Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Identity Simplification", "Section"], 
   Cell["No neural network is used below. Each diagram is reduced with its own two internal \
numerator mass-shell conditions before the diagrams are summed. Original propagator denominators \
stay off shell throughout. All particles are ingoing.", "Text"], 
   Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Definitions", "Subsection"], Cell["ClearAll[q5Angle, q5Square, \
q5Mixed, q5K, q5A, q5B, q5Route];\nq5Angle[i_, j_] := ReduceSpinorProducts[SpinorChain[\n  \
Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Angle\", i], Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Angle\", j]]];\nq5Square[i_, j_] := \
ReduceSpinorProducts[SpinorChain[\n  Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Square\", i], Spinor[\"Helicity\", \
\"Square\", j]]];\nq5Mixed[i_, p_, j_] := ReduceSpinorProducts[SpinorChain[\n  Spinor[\"Helicity\", \
\"Angle\", i], Mom[p], Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Square\", j]]];\nq5K[i_] := \
SpinorChain[Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Square\", i], Mom[1], Mom[2],\n  Spinor[\"Helicity\", \
\"Square\", i]];\nq5A[i_] := PropDen[Mom[Multiparticle[1, i]], Me];\nq5B[i_] := \
PropDen[Mom[Multiparticle[2, i]], Me];\n\nq5Route[pair_] := Module[{massRules = First[pair], raw, \
order, aa, bb, cc,\n    references, referenceState, conserved, contracted, determinant, shell,\n    \
auxiliaryDenominators, result, product, determinantRule, stages},\n  raw = \
ReduceSpinContractions[Last[pair]] /. massRules;\n  order = Table[First[Cases[raw,\n    \
SpinorChain[Spinor[\"Xi\", \"Angle\", 9 + v], Mom[_],\n      Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Square\", \
photon_]] :> photon, Infinity]], {v, 3}];\n  {aa, bb, cc} = order;\n  references = {Spinor[\"Xi\", \
\"Angle\", 10] -> Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Angle\", bb],\n    Spinor[\"Xi\", \"Angle\", 11] -> \
Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Angle\", aa]};\n  referenceState = raw /. references /. {\n    \
SpinorChain[Spinor[\"Xi\", \"Angle\", 12], tail__] :>\n      SpinorChain[Spinor[\"Helicity\", \
\"Square\", cc], Mom[1], tail]};\n  conserved = referenceState /. {\n    \
SpinorChain[Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Angle\", bb], Mom[_Multiparticle],\n        Spinor[\"Helicity\", \
\"Square\", aa]] :>\n      -SpinorChain[Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Angle\", bb], Mom[1] + Mom[aa],\n    \
    Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Square\", aa]],\n    SpinorChain[Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Angle\", aa], \
Mom[_Multiparticle],\n        Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Square\", bb]] :>\n      \
-SpinorChain[Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Angle\", aa], Mom[1] + Mom[aa] + Mom[bb],\n        \
Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Square\", bb]]};\n  contracted = ReduceSpinorProducts[conserved] /. \
massRules;\n  product = q5Mixed[bb, 1, aa] q5Mixed[aa, 1, bb];\n  determinantRule = With[{lhs = \
product,\n      rhs = Me^2 q5Angle[aa, bb] q5Square[aa, bb] +\n        q5Mixed[aa, 1, aa] \
q5Mixed[bb, 1, bb]}, lhs -> rhs];\n  determinant = Expand[contracted /. determinantRule];\n  shell \
= Factor[determinant /. q5Mixed[aa, 1, aa] -> 0];\n  (* Only auxiliary spinor denominators are \
converted. Original PropDen\n     factors remain opaque and off shell. *)\n  auxiliaryDenominators \
= shell /.\n    q5Mixed[cc, 1, cc] -> q5A[cc] /.\n    With[{angle = q5Angle @@ Sort[{aa, bb}], \
square = q5Square @@ Sort[{aa, bb}], den = q5A[bb]},\n      Power[angle, -1] -> square/den];\n  \
result = Factor[auxiliaryDenominators /.\n    PropDen[Mom[Multiparticle @@ Sort[{1, aa, bb}]], Me] \
-> q5B[cc]];\n  stages = <|\"Raw\" -> raw, \"ReferenceSpinors\" -> referenceState,\n    \
\"MomentumConservation\" -> conserved, \"MasslessEndpointContractions\" -> contracted,\n    \
\"DeterminantSchouten\" -> determinant, \"FirstInternalOnShell\" -> shell,\n    \
\"SecondInternalOnShellAndAuxiliaryDenominators\" -> auxiliaryDenominators,\n    \
\"ComplementaryPropagatorMomentum\" -> result|>;\n  <|\"PhotonOrder\" -> order, \"MassRules\" -> \
massRules,\n    \"NumeratorShells\" -> {Multiparticle[1, aa], Multiparticle[2, cc]},\n    \
\"Stages\" -> stages, \"Result\" -> result|>\n];", "Input"]}, Closed]], 
   Cell["Six Photon Orderings", "Subsection"], Cell["For an ordering (a,b,c), the internal momenta \
are p1+pa and -(p2+pc). Their numerator conditions are (p1+pa)^2=Me^2 and (p2+pc)^2=Me^2. A_i \
denotes PropDen[p1+pi,Me], B_i denotes PropDen[p2+pi,Me], and K_i denotes [i|p1 p2|i]. These A_i \
and B_i are never set to zero.", "Text"], Cell["q5Input = diagramAmplitudes[diags];\nq5Routes = \
q5Route /@ q5Input;\nGrid[Prepend[({#[\"PhotonOrder\"], #[\"NumeratorShells\"], #[\"Result\"]} & /@ \
q5Routes),\n  {\"Photon Order\", \"Numerator Shells\", \"Reduced Diagram\"}], Alignment -> Left]", 
    "Input"], Cell["The determinant form of Schouten gives <b|p1|a]<a|p1|b] - <a|p1|a]<b|p1|b] = \
Me^2 <ab>[ab]. The first internal shell removes <a|p1|a]. The second internal shell gives \
<ab>[ab]=2 p1.pb. Choosing the third reference spinor to be [c|p1 gives K_c/(2 p1.pc). This removes \
all reference spinors. Only the auxiliary reference denominators are rewritten; the original \
diagram propagators are untouched.", "Text"], 
   Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Detailed Route", "Subsection"], Cell["q5Example = \
1;\nq5Routes[[q5Example]][\"PhotonOrder\"]\nGrid[KeyValueMap[{#1, #2} &, \
q5Routes[[q5Example]][\"Stages\"]], Alignment -> Left]", "Input"]}, Closed]], 
   Cell["Combined Result", "Subsection"], Cell["The two orders with the same rightmost photon give \
the same reduced expression. Their six contributions therefore combine into the three terms below. \
q5Final is the factored result; q5FinalCommon is the same result as one rational fraction.", 
    "Text"], Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["q5Spin =SpinorChain[Spinor[\"Spin\", \"Angle\", 1], \
Spinor[\"Spin\", \"Angle\", 2]];\nq5Final = 4 Sqrt[2] EE^3 Me q5Spin/(q5A[3] q5A[4] q5A[5]) *\n  \
(q5Square[4, 5]^2 q5K[3]/q5B[3] + q5Square[3, 5]^2 q5K[4]/q5B[4] +\n    q5Square[3, 4]^2 \
q5K[5]/q5B[5]);\nq5FinalCommon = Together[q5Final];\nq5Final", "Input"], 
      Cell[BoxData[FractionBox[RowBox[{"4", " ", SqrtBox["2"], " ", SuperscriptBox["EE", "3"], " ", 
           "Me", " ", TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"〈\"", StyleBox["1", Bold, StripOnInput -> 
                 False]}, "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[{StyleBox["2", Bold, StripOnInput -> False], 
               "\"〉\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"], " ", 
           RowBox[{"(", RowBox[{FractionBox[RowBox[{SuperscriptBox[TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[
                      {"\"[\"", "4"}, "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[{"5", "\"]\""}, "RowDefault"]}, 
                    "RowDefault"], "2"], " ", TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"[\"", "3"}, 
                     "RowDefault"], "\"|\"", SubscriptBox["p", "1"], SubscriptBox["p", "2"], 
                    "\"|\"", TemplateBox[{"3", "\"]\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"]}], 
                RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], "+", SubsuperscriptBox["p", 
                   RowBox[{"2", ",", "3"}], "2"]}]], "+", FractionBox[RowBox[{SuperscriptBox[
                   TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"[\"", "3"}, "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[
                      {"5", "\"]\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"], "2"], " ", TemplateBox[
                   {TemplateBox[{"\"[\"", "4"}, "RowDefault"], "\"|\"", SubscriptBox["p", "1"], 
                    SubscriptBox["p", "2"], "\"|\"", TemplateBox[{"4", "\"]\""}, "RowDefault"]}, 
                   "RowDefault"]}], RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], "+", 
                  SubsuperscriptBox["p", RowBox[{"2", ",", "4"}], "2"]}]], "+", FractionBox[
                RowBox[{SuperscriptBox[TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"[\"", "3"}, "RowDefault"], 
                     TemplateBox[{"4", "\"]\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"], "2"], " ", 
                  TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"[\"", "5"}, "RowDefault"], "\"|\"", SubscriptBox[
                     "p", "1"], SubscriptBox["p", "2"], "\"|\"", TemplateBox[{"5", "\"]\""}, 
                     "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"]}], RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", 
                     "2"]}], "+", SubsuperscriptBox["p", RowBox[{"2", ",", "5"}], "2"]}]]}], 
             ")"}]}], RowBox[{RowBox[{"(", RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], "+", 
               SubsuperscriptBox["p", RowBox[{"1", ",", "3"}], "2"]}], ")"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"(", RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], "+", SubsuperscriptBox[
                "p", RowBox[{"1", ",", "4"}], "2"]}], ")"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"(", RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], "+", SubsuperscriptBox[
                "p", RowBox[{"1", ",", "5"}], "2"]}], ")"}]}]]], "Output"]}, Open]], 
   Cell["q5RouteChecks =Map[Function[route, With[{aa = route[\"PhotonOrder\"][[1]],\n    bb = \
route[\"PhotonOrder\"][[2]], cc = route[\"PhotonOrder\"][[3]]},\n  Together[route[\"Result\"] - 2 \
Sqrt[2] EE^3 Me q5Spin q5Square[aa, bb]^2 q5K[cc]/\n    (q5A[3] q5A[4] q5A[5] q5B[cc])] === 0]], \
q5Routes];\nq5SumCheck = Together[Total[Lookup[q5Routes, \"Result\"]] - q5Final] === \
0;\n<|\"SixRoutes\" -> q5RouteChecks, \"Sum\" -> q5SumCheck,\n  \"NoReferenceSpinors\" -> \
FreeQ[q5Final, Spinor[\"Xi\", ___]],\n  \"NoInversePhotonAngleBrackets\" -> \
FreeQ[Denominator[Together[q5Final]],\n    SpinorChain[Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Angle\", _], \
Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Angle\", _]]]|>", "Input"], 
   Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Independent Algebraic Checks", "Subsection"], 
      Cell["This check uses arbitrary two-component spinors and exact algebra. It proves reference \
independence with both internal numerator shells, and proves equality of the final form with its \
p1/p2-reflected representation using external shells alone. The original PropDen factors cancel out \
of these numerator checks and are not evaluated. Separately, 94 nondegenerate exact checks of the \
actual six generated diagrams passed, with four masses and independently varied references. These \
are checks of the stated constructive numerator prescription, not a separate comparison with \
off-shell Feynman matrix elements.", "Text"], Cell["ClearAll[q5VerifyIdentities];\nq5VerifyIdentiti\
es[] := Module[{eps, adj, la, lb, lc, ta, tb, tc, p1, p2,\n    pa, pb, pc, ad, bd, kin, weights, \
endpoint, externalRule, cutRules,\n    cutExternalRule, rawProduct, reducedProduct, check, a, b, d, \
m, u, v,\n    r, s, t, w, z1, z2, z3, z4, z5, z6},\n  eps = {{0, 1}, {-1, 0}};\n  adj[p_] := \
{{p[[2, 2]], -p[[1, 2]]}, {-p[[2, 1]], p[[1, 1]]}};\n  la = {1, 0}; lb = {0, 1}; lc = {u, v};\n  ta \
= {1, 0}; tb = {r, s}; tc = {t, w};\n  p1 = {{a, b}, {d, (m^2 + b d)/a}};\n  pa = -Outer[Times, la, \
ta.eps];\n  pb = -Outer[Times, lb, tb.eps];\n  pc = -Outer[Times, lc, tc.eps];\n  p2 = -p1 - pa - \
pb - pc;\n  externalRule = First[Solve[Det[p2] == m^2, t]];\n  ad = {Det[p1 + pa] - m^2, Det[p1 + \
pb] - m^2, Det[p1 + pc] - m^2};\n  bd = {Det[p2 + pa] - m^2, Det[p2 + pb] - m^2, Det[p2 + pc] - \
m^2};\n  kin = (-#.eps.adj[p1].p2.# &) /@ {ta, tb, tc};\n  weights = {(-tb.eps.tc)^2, \
(-ta.eps.tc)^2, (-ta.eps.tb)^2};\n  endpoint = Total[Table[weights[[i]] kin[[i]] *\n    ((Times @@ \
Delete[bd, i]) - (Times @@ Delete[ad, i])), {i, 3}]];\n  cutRules = {d -> 0, r -> -(b - 1) s/a};\n  \
cutExternalRule = First[Solve[\n    Together[(Det[p2] - m^2) /. cutRules] == 0, t]];\n  rawProduct \
= -({z1, z2}.eps.p1.ta)/({z1, z2}.eps.la) *\n    ({z3, z4}.eps.(p2 + pc).tb)/({z3, z4}.eps.lb) *\n  \
  ({z5, z6}.eps.p2.tc)/({z5, z6}.eps.lc);\n  reducedProduct = -m^2 weights[[3]] kin[[3]]/(ad[[2]] \
ad[[3]]);\n  check[x_] := Together[x /. cutRules /. cutExternalRule] === 0;\n  \
<|\"ExternalMassShells\" ->\n      AllTrue[Together[{Det[p1] - m^2, Det[p2] - m^2} /. \
externalRule], # === 0 &],\n    \"BothInternalNumeratorShells\" ->\n      (check[ad[[1]]] && \
check[bd[[3]]]),\n    \"ArbitraryReferenceSpinors\" -> check[rawProduct - reducedProduct],\n    \
\"ReflectedFinalForm\" -> (Together[endpoint /. externalRule] === 0)|>\n];\nq5VerifyIdentities[]", 
       "Input"]}, Closed]]}, Open]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Cyclic Reference Spinors", "Section"], 
   Cell["This is a separate derivation. The earlier sections and q5Final are unchanged. Evaluate \
Setup and the preceding Definitions first. For photon order (a,b,c), choose \
(Xi10,Xi11,Xi12)=(b,c,a). Thus the first diagram uses exactly (4,5,3). None of these reference \
spinors contains a momentum insertion.", "Text"], 
   Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Cyclic Route Definitions", "Subsection"], 
      Cell["ClearAll[q5CyclicRoute];\nq5CyclicRoute[pair_] := Module[{raw, massRules = First[pair], \
order, aa, bb, cc,\n    referenceState, referenceSchouten, internalReferenceCondition, \
equivalentReference,\n    conserved, contracted, product, determinant, firstShell, result, stages, \
qq},\n  raw = ReduceSpinContractions[Last[pair]] /. massRules;\n  order = Table[First[Cases[raw,\n  \
  SpinorChain[Spinor[\"Xi\", \"Angle\", 9 + v], Mom[_],\n      Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Square\", \
photon_]] :> photon, Infinity]], {v, 3}];\n  {aa, bb, cc} = order;\n  qq = Multiparticle @@ \
Sort[{2, cc}];\n  referenceState = raw /. Thread[Table[Spinor[\"Xi\", \"Angle\", 9 + v], {v, 3}] \
->\n    (Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Angle\", #] & /@ {bb, cc, aa})];\n  referenceSchouten = \
referenceState /.\n    SpinorChain[Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Angle\", cc], Mom[qq],\n      \
Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Square\", bb]] ->\n      (q5Angle[cc, bb]/q5Angle[aa, bb] *\n        \
SpinorChain[Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Angle\", aa], Mom[qq],\n          Spinor[\"Helicity\", \
\"Square\", bb]] -\n       q5Angle[cc, aa]/q5Angle[aa, bb] *\n        \
SpinorChain[Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Angle\", bb], Mom[qq],\n          Spinor[\"Helicity\", \
\"Square\", bb]]);\n  internalReferenceCondition = Expand[referenceSchouten /.\n    \
SpinorChain[Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Angle\", bb], Mom[qq],\n      Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Square\", \
bb]] -> q5A[aa] - q5B[cc]];\n  equivalentReference = referenceSchouten /.\n    \
SpinorChain[Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Angle\", bb], Mom[qq],\n      Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Square\", \
bb]] -> 0;\n  conserved = equivalentReference /. {\n    SpinorChain[Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Angle\", \
bb], Mom[_Multiparticle],\n        Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Square\", aa]] :>\n      \
-SpinorChain[Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Angle\", bb], Mom[1] + Mom[aa],\n        Spinor[\"Helicity\", \
\"Square\", aa]],\n    SpinorChain[Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Angle\", aa], Mom[qq],\n        \
Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Square\", bb]] :>\n      -SpinorChain[Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Angle\", aa], \
Mom[1] + Mom[aa] + Mom[bb],\n        Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Square\", bb]]};\n  contracted = \
Expand[conserved /. chain_SpinorChain :> ReduceSpinorProducts[chain]] /. massRules;\n  product = \
q5Mixed[bb, 1, aa] q5Mixed[aa, 1, bb];\n  determinant = Expand[contracted /. With[{lhs = product,\n \
     rhs = Me^2 q5Angle[aa, bb] q5Square[aa, bb] +\n        q5Mixed[aa, 1, aa] q5Mixed[bb, 1, bb]}, \
lhs -> rhs]];\n  firstShell = Factor[determinant /. q5Mixed[aa, 1, aa] -> 0];\n  result = \
Factor[firstShell /.\n    PropDen[Mom[Multiparticle @@ Sort[{1, aa, bb}]], Me] -> q5B[cc]];\n  \
stages = <|\"Raw\" -> raw, \"CyclicReferenceSpinors\" -> referenceState,\n    \"ReferenceSchouten\" \
-> referenceSchouten,\n    \"ReferenceChangeRemainderBeforeCut\" -> internalReferenceCondition,\n   \
 \"BothInternalShellsForReferenceChange\" -> equivalentReference,\n    \"MomentumConservation\" -> \
conserved, \"MasslessEndpointContractions\" -> contracted,\n    \"DeterminantSchouten\" -> \
determinant, \"FirstInternalNumeratorShell\" -> firstShell,\n    \
\"ComplementaryPropagatorMomentum\" -> result|>;\n  <|\"PhotonOrder\" -> order, \"References\" -> \
{bb, cc, aa},\n    \"NumeratorShells\" -> {Multiparticle[1, aa], Multiparticle[2, cc]},\n    \
\"Stages\" -> stages, \"Result\" -> result|>\n];", "Input"]}, Closed]], 
   Cell["q5CyclicInput = diagramAmplitudes[diags];\nq5CyclicRoutes = q5CyclicRoute /@ \
q5CyclicInput;\nq5CyclicRoutes[[1]][\"References\"]", "Input"], 
   Cell["The middle reference is changed using the two-dimensional Schouten identity. For Q=p2+pc, \
Y(c,Q,b) = <cb> Y(a,Q,b)/<ab> - <ca> Y(b,Q,b)/<ab>. External equal-mass shells and momentum \
conservation give Y(b,Q,b)=A_a-B_c. Both internal numerator shells therefore remove the second \
term. This step does not set either original propagator denominator to zero.", "Text"], 
   Cell["Conservation and massless endpoint contractions then leave the product <b|p1|a]<a|p1|b]. \
Its determinant-Schouten identity and the first internal numerator shell reduce the diagram to the \
expression below. In particular, the first ordering gives [34]<3|p2|5]/(<34><35>A_3 B_5), \
multiplied by 2 Sqrt[2] EE^3 Me <bold1 bold2>.", "Text"], 
   Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["q5CyclicRoutes[[1]][\"Result\"]", "Input"], 
      Cell[BoxData[FractionBox[RowBox[{"2", " ", SqrtBox["2"], " ", SuperscriptBox["EE", "3"], " ", 
           "Me", " ", TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"[\"", "3"}, "RowDefault"], 
             TemplateBox[{"4", "\"]\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"], " ", 
           TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"〈\"", StyleBox["1", Bold, StripOnInput -> False]}, 
              "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[{StyleBox["2", Bold, StripOnInput -> False], "\"〉\""}, 
              "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"], " ", TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"[\"", "5"}, 
              "RowDefault"], "\"|\"", SubscriptBox["p", "2"], "\"|\"", TemplateBox[
              {"3", "\"〉\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"]}], 
         RowBox[{RowBox[{"(", RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], "+", 
               SubsuperscriptBox["p", RowBox[{"1", ",", "3"}], "2"]}], ")"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"(", RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], "+", SubsuperscriptBox[
                "p", RowBox[{"2", ",", "5"}], "2"]}], ")"}], " ", TemplateBox[
            {TemplateBox[{"\"〈\"", "3"}, "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[{"4", "\"〉\""}, 
              "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"], " ", TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"〈\"", "3"}, 
              "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[{"5", "\"〉\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"]}]]], 
       "Output"]}, Open]], Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["All Six Routes", "Subsection"], 
      Cell["Grid[Prepend[({#[\"PhotonOrder\"], #[\"References\"], #[\"Result\"]} & /@ \
q5CyclicRoutes),\n  {\"Photon Order\", \"References\", \"Reduced Diagram\"}], Alignment -> \
Left]\nq5CyclicExample = 1;\nGrid[KeyValueMap[{#1, #2} &, \
q5CyclicRoutes[[q5CyclicExample]][\"Stages\"]], Alignment -> Left]", "Input"]}, Closed]]}, Open]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Cyclic Sum and Pole Cancellation", "Section"], 
   Cell["Sum the six inverse-angle expressions before applying further identities. No internal \
shell condition is imposed on this combined sum. External shells, conservation, Schouten, and \
K_c=[ac]<a|p2|c]+[bc]<b|p2|c] cancel the inverse photon-angle poles. The cancellation involves the \
complete sum, not each pair of orders separately.", "Text"], 
   Cell["q5CyclicSum = Total[Lookup[q5CyclicRoutes, \"Result\"]];\nq5CyclicSum", "Input"], 
   Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["q5CyclicSpin = SpinorChain[Spinor[\"Spin\", \"Angle\", 1], \
Spinor[\"Spin\", \"Angle\", 2]];\nq5CyclicSum = Total[Lookup[q5CyclicRoutes, \
\"Result\"]];\nq5CyclicFinal = 2 Sqrt[2] EE^3 Me q5CyclicSpin/(q5A[3] q5A[4] q5A[5]) *\n  \
(q5Square[4, 5]^2 q5K[3]/q5B[3] + q5Square[3, 5]^2 q5K[4]/q5B[4] +\n    q5Square[3, 4]^2 \
q5K[5]/q5B[5]);\nq5CyclicFinalCommon = Together[q5CyclicFinal];\nq5CyclicFinal", "Input"], 
      Cell[BoxData[FractionBox[RowBox[{"2", " ", SqrtBox["2"], " ", SuperscriptBox["EE", "3"], " ", 
           "Me", " ", TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"〈\"", StyleBox["1", Bold, StripOnInput -> 
                 False]}, "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[{StyleBox["2", Bold, StripOnInput -> False], 
               "\"〉\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"], " ", 
           RowBox[{"(", RowBox[{FractionBox[RowBox[{SuperscriptBox[TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[
                      {"\"[\"", "4"}, "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[{"5", "\"]\""}, "RowDefault"]}, 
                    "RowDefault"], "2"], " ", TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"[\"", "3"}, 
                     "RowDefault"], "\"|\"", SubscriptBox["p", "1"], SubscriptBox["p", "2"], 
                    "\"|\"", TemplateBox[{"3", "\"]\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"]}], 
                RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], "+", SubsuperscriptBox["p", 
                   RowBox[{"2", ",", "3"}], "2"]}]], "+", FractionBox[RowBox[{SuperscriptBox[
                   TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"[\"", "3"}, "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[
                      {"5", "\"]\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"], "2"], " ", TemplateBox[
                   {TemplateBox[{"\"[\"", "4"}, "RowDefault"], "\"|\"", SubscriptBox["p", "1"], 
                    SubscriptBox["p", "2"], "\"|\"", TemplateBox[{"4", "\"]\""}, "RowDefault"]}, 
                   "RowDefault"]}], RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], "+", 
                  SubsuperscriptBox["p", RowBox[{"2", ",", "4"}], "2"]}]], "+", FractionBox[
                RowBox[{SuperscriptBox[TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"[\"", "3"}, "RowDefault"], 
                     TemplateBox[{"4", "\"]\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"], "2"], " ", 
                  TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"[\"", "5"}, "RowDefault"], "\"|\"", SubscriptBox[
                     "p", "1"], SubscriptBox["p", "2"], "\"|\"", TemplateBox[{"5", "\"]\""}, 
                     "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"]}], RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", 
                     "2"]}], "+", SubsuperscriptBox["p", RowBox[{"2", ",", "5"}], "2"]}]]}], 
             ")"}]}], RowBox[{RowBox[{"(", RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], "+", 
               SubsuperscriptBox["p", RowBox[{"1", ",", "3"}], "2"]}], ")"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"(", RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], "+", SubsuperscriptBox[
                "p", RowBox[{"1", ",", "4"}], "2"]}], ")"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"(", RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], "+", SubsuperscriptBox[
                "p", RowBox[{"1", ",", "5"}], "2"]}], ")"}]}]]], "Output"]}, Open]], 
   Cell[TextData[{StyleBox["Factor-of-Two Discrepancy", FontWeight -> "Bold"], "\nThe cyclic result \
is exactly q5Final/2, not q5Final. Its spurious poles cancel, but it is not the same off-shell \
function as the earlier physical-reference result. Both results are retained. No normalization has \
been adjusted to force agreement."}], "Text"], Cell["q5CyclicRouteChecks = Map[Function[route, \
With[{aa = route[\"PhotonOrder\"][[1]],\n    bb = route[\"PhotonOrder\"][[2]], cc = \
route[\"PhotonOrder\"][[3]]},\n  Together[route[\"Result\"] - 2 Sqrt[2] EE^3 Me q5CyclicSpin *\n    \
q5Square[aa, bb] q5Mixed[aa, 2, cc]/\n    (q5Angle[aa, bb] q5Angle[aa, cc] q5A[aa] q5B[cc])] === \
0]], q5CyclicRoutes];\n<|\"SixCyclicRoutes\" -> q5CyclicRouteChecks,\n  \"EqualToPreviousResult\" \
-> (Together[q5CyclicFinal - q5Final] === 0),\n  \"EqualToHalfPreviousResult\" -> \
(Together[q5CyclicFinal - q5Final/2] === 0)|>", "Input"], 
   Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Exact Pole-Cancellation Proof", "Subsection"], 
      Cell["The check below uses generic symbolic two-component spinors with only the external \
equal-mass conditions and momentum conservation. It proves the six-term cyclic sum equals the new \
three-term expression. It also verifies the exact discarded remainder of each of the six diagrams. \
EqualToPreviousResult is expected to be False; EqualsHalfPreviousResult is expected to be True.", 
       "Text"], Cell["ClearAll[q5VerifyCyclic];\nq5VerifyCyclic[] := Module[{eps, adj, lam, til, \
pm, p1, p2, extRule, angle,\n    square, y, ad, bd, kin, orders, summands, physical, rawProducts, \
remainders,\n    reducedProducts, fullDenominator, checkExternal, sumCheck, remainderChecks,\n    \
a, b, d, m, u, v, r, s, t, w},\n  eps = {{0, 1}, {-1, 0}};\n  adj[p_] := {{p[[2, 2]], -p[[1, 2]]}, \
{-p[[2, 1]], p[[1, 1]]}};\n  lam[3] = {1, 0}; lam[4] = {0, 1}; lam[5] = {u, v};\n  til[3] = {1, 0}; \
til[4] = {r, s}; til[5] = {t, w};\n  pm[i_] := Outer[Times, lam[i], til[i]];\n  p1 = {{a, b}, {d, \
(m^2 + b d)/a}};\n  p2 = -p1 - Total[pm /@ {3, 4, 5}];\n  extRule = First[Solve[Det[p2] == m^2, \
t]];\n  angle[i_, j_] := -lam[i].eps.lam[j];\n  square[i_, j_] := til[i].eps.til[j];\n  y[i_, p_, \
j_] := -lam[i].eps.p.eps.til[j];\n  ad[i_] := Det[p1 + pm[i]] - m^2;\n  bd[i_] := Det[p2 + pm[i]] - \
m^2;\n  kin[i_] := til[i].adj[p1].p2.eps.til[i];\n  orders = Permutations[{3, 4, 5}];\n  summands = \
Function[ord, With[{aa = ord[[1]], bb = ord[[2]], cc = ord[[3]]},\n    square[aa, bb] y[aa, p2, \
cc]/\n      (angle[aa, bb] angle[aa, cc] ad[aa] bd[cc])]] /@ orders;\n  physical = \
Total[Function[cc, With[{pair = Complement[{3, 4, 5}, {cc}]},\n    (square @@ pair)^2 \
kin[cc]/bd[cc]]] /@ {3, 4, 5}]/\n    (ad[3] ad[4] ad[5]);\n  rawProducts = Function[ord, With[{aa = \
ord[[1]], bb = ord[[2]], cc = ord[[3]]},\n    -y[bb, p1, aa]/angle[bb, aa] * y[cc, p2 + pm[cc], \
bb]/angle[cc, bb] *\n      y[aa, p2, cc]/angle[aa, cc]]] /@ orders;\n  reducedProducts = \
Function[ord, With[{aa = ord[[1]], bb = ord[[2]], cc = ord[[3]]},\n    -m^2 square[aa, bb] y[aa, \
p2, cc]/(angle[aa, bb] angle[aa, cc])]] /@ orders;\n  remainders = Function[ord, With[{aa = \
ord[[1]], bb = ord[[2]], cc = ord[[3]]},\n    y[aa, p2, cc] * (angle[aa, cc] y[bb, p1, aa] (bd[cc] \
- ad[aa]) -\n      angle[bb, cc] ad[aa] ad[bb])/\n      (angle[aa, bb]^2 angle[aa, cc] angle[bb, \
cc])]] /@ orders;\n  checkExternal[x_] := Together[x /. extRule] === 0;\n  fullDenominator = Times \
@@ Join[ad /@ {3, 4, 5}, bd /@ {3, 4, 5}];\n  sumCheck = checkExternal[(Total[summands] - physical) \
fullDenominator];\n  remainderChecks = checkExternal /@ (rawProducts - reducedProducts - \
remainders);\n  <|\"ExternalMassShells\" -> (checkExternal[Det[p1] - m^2] &&\n      \
checkExternal[Det[p2] - m^2]),\n    \"CyclicSumEqualsNewPhysicalPoleForm\" -> sumCheck,\n    \
\"SpuriousAnglePolesCancel\" -> sumCheck,\n    \"ExactDiscardedRemainders\" -> remainderChecks,\n   \
 \"MatchesPreviousResult\" -> checkExternal[Total[summands] - 2 physical],\n    \
\"EqualsHalfPreviousResult\" -> sumCheck|>\n];\nq5CyclicProof = q5VerifyCyclic[];\nq5CyclicProof", 
       "Input"]}, Closed]]}, Open]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Reference Choice and Off-Shell Completion", "Section"], 
   Cell["Let P_abc denote the original product of the three reference-spinor ratios, before the \
overall factor -2 Sqrt[2] EE^3 <bold1 bold2>/(Me A_a B_c). The exact identity is P_abc = -Me^2 \
[ab]<a|p2|c]/(<ab><ac>) + R_abc, with the remainder below. This identity is verified under external \
shells without putting the internal lines on shell.", "Text"], 
   Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["ClearAll[q5CyclicRemainder];\nq5CyclicRemainder[aa_, bb_, cc_] := \
q5Mixed[aa, 2, cc] *\n  (q5Angle[aa, cc] q5Mixed[bb, 1, aa] (q5B[cc] - q5A[aa]) -\n    q5Angle[bb, \
cc] q5A[aa] q5A[bb])/\n  (q5Angle[aa, bb]^2 q5Angle[aa, cc] q5Angle[bb, cc]);\nq5CyclicRemainder[3, \
4, 5]", "Input"]}, Open]], Cell["R_abc vanishes when both internal numerator conditions A_a=B_c=0 \
hold. However, dividing it by the off-shell original propagators A_a B_c produces terms with a \
single propagator or no original propagators. These terms need not vanish in the full amplitude. \
This is why reference independence on an individual double cut does not by itself determine a \
unique amplitude away from the cut. The factor-of-two discrepancy is unresolved physically; an \
independent amplitude or factorization check is needed to choose the completion, rather than \
multiplying one result by two.", "Text"], Cell["Independent exact checks of all six generated \
diagrams, at four masses, passed for the cyclic reference choice and its reduced numerator. \
Original PropDen factors were kept opaque. These 24 cut checks validate the identities but do not \
decide the off-shell completion or its normalization.", "Text"]}, Open]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Common Reference Spinor", "Section"], 
   Cell["Use one arbitrary angle reference Xi for all three photons in every diagram. Require <Xi \
3>, <Xi 4>, and <Xi 5> to be nonzero. This section is independent of the earlier reference \
prescriptions and preserves both previous results. Evaluate Setup and the preceding Identity \
Simplification definitions first.", "Text"], 
   Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Common-Reference Route Definitions", "Subsection"], 
      Cell["ClearAll[q5CommonXi, q5Z, q5CommonY, q5CommonRoute];\nq5CommonXi = Spinor[\"Xi\", \
\"Angle\", 0];\nq5Z[i_] := SpinorChain[q5CommonXi, Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Angle\", \
i]];\nq5CommonY[p_, i_] := SpinorChain[q5CommonXi, Mom[p],\n  Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Square\", \
i]];\nq5CommonRoute[pair_] := Module[{raw, refs, order, a, b, c, u, v, y,\n    f, f0, delta, \
commonProduct, cyclicProduct, remainder, spin, reduced, stages},\n  raw = \
ReduceSpinContractions[Last[pair]] /. First[pair];\n  order = Table[First[Cases[raw,\n    \
SpinorChain[Spinor[\"Xi\", \"Angle\", 9 + n], Mom[_],\n      Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Square\", i_]] \
:> i, Infinity]], {n, 3}];\n  {a, b, c} = order;\n  refs = raw /. Spinor[\"Xi\", \"Angle\", _] -> \
q5CommonXi;\n  u = q5Mixed[b, 1, a]; v = q5Mixed[a, 1, b]; y = q5Mixed[a, 2, c];\n  f = \
{-q5CommonY[1, a]/q5Z[a],\n    (q5CommonY[2, b] + q5Z[c] q5Square[c, b])/q5Z[b],\n    q5CommonY[2, \
c]/q5Z[c]};\n  f0 = {u/q5Angle[a, b], -v/q5Angle[a, b], y/q5Angle[a, c]};\n  delta = {-q5Z[b] \
q5A[a]/(q5Angle[a, b] q5Z[a]),\n    -q5Z[a] (q5A[a] - q5B[c])/(q5Angle[a, b] q5Z[b]),\n    -q5Z[a] \
q5B[c]/(q5Angle[a, c] q5Z[c])};\n  commonProduct = Times @@ f;\n  cyclicProduct = -Me^2 q5Square[a, \
b] y/(q5Angle[a, b] q5Angle[a, c]);\n  remainder = delta[[1]] f[[2]] f[[3]] + f0[[1]] delta[[2]] \
f[[3]] +\n    f0[[1]] f0[[2]] delta[[3]] -\n    q5A[a] q5A[b] y/(q5Angle[a, b]^2 q5Angle[a, c]);\n  \
spin = SpinorChain[Spinor[\"Spin\", \"Angle\", 1], Spinor[\"Spin\", \"Angle\", 2]];\n  reduced = 2 \
Sqrt[2] EE^3 Me spin q5Square[a, b] y/\n    (q5Angle[a, b] q5Angle[a, c] q5A[a] q5B[c]);\n  stages \
= <|\"RawCommonReference\" -> refs,\n    \"ConservationAndMasslessEndpoints\" -> f,\n    \
\"ReferenceChangeTerms\" -> delta,\n    \"OnCutFactors\" -> f0,\n    \"DeterminantSchouten\" -> (u \
v == Me^2 q5Angle[a, b] q5Square[a, b] +\n      q5A[a] q5A[b]),\n    \"OnCutProduct\" -> \
cyclicProduct,\n    \"ExactRemainder\" -> remainder,\n    \"ReducedDiagram\" -> reduced|>;\n  \
<|\"PhotonOrder\" -> order, \"CommonReference\" -> q5CommonXi,\n    \"NumeratorShells\" -> \
{Multiparticle[1, a], Multiparticle[2, c]},\n    \"Raw\" -> refs, \"Product\" -> commonProduct, \
\"Result\" -> reduced,\n    \"Remainder\" -> remainder, \"Stages\" -> stages|>\n];", "Input"]}, 
     Closed]], Cell["Six Diagrams With One Xi", "Subsection"], 
   Cell["q5CommonInput = diagramAmplitudes[diags];\nq5CommonRoutes = q5CommonRoute /@ \
q5CommonInput;\nq5CommonRawSum = Total[Lookup[q5CommonRoutes, \"Raw\"]];\nq5CommonReducedSum = \
Total[Lookup[q5CommonRoutes, \"Result\"]];\nGrid[Prepend[({#[\"PhotonOrder\"], \
#[\"CommonReference\"], #[\"Result\"]} & /@ q5CommonRoutes),\n  {\"Photon Order\", \"Common Xi\", \
\"Reduced Diagram\"}], Alignment -> Left]", "Input"], 
   Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Detailed Numerator Route", "Subsection"], 
      Cell["Define zeta_i=<Xi i>, U=<b|p1|a], V=<a|p1|b], Y=<a|p2|c], and Q=p2+pc. Conservation and \
massless endpoint contractions give F1=-<Xi|p1|a]/zeta_a, F2=<Xi|Q|b]/zeta_b, F3=<Xi|p2|c]/zeta_c. \
Their product is the original numerator ratio P_abc. The original propagators remain A_a B_c.", 
       "Text"], Cell["Schouten gives F=C+delta with C={U/<ab>,-V/<ab>,Y/<ac>} and delta={-zeta_b \
A_a/(<ab> zeta_a), zeta_a(B_c-A_a)/(<ab> zeta_b), -zeta_a B_c/(<ac> zeta_c)}. Each delta vanishes \
on this diagram's two internal numerator shells. Determinant-Schouten gives UV=Me^2<ab>[ab]+A_a \
A_b. Thus P_abc=-Me^2[ab]Y/(<ab><ac>)+R_abc.", "Text"], Cell["The exact remainder is displayed \
without expanding its products: R_abc=-A_a A_b Y/(<ab>^2<ac>)+delta1 F2 F3+C1 delta2 F3+C1 C2 \
delta3. Every term carries A_a or B_c, so it vanishes on that diagram's double cut. Do not set \
either original propagator to zero. We keep the remainder until checking its contribution to the \
complete sum.", "Text"], Cell["q5CommonExample = 1;\nGrid[KeyValueMap[{#1, #2} &, \
q5CommonRoutes[[q5CommonExample]][\"Stages\"]],\n  Alignment -> Left]", "Input"]}, Closed]], 
   Cell["Reference Cancellation And Equivalence", "Subsection"], 
   Cell["The cancellation is proved for a generic symbolic common Xi=(alpha,beta), not for a single \
numerical choice. In the same generic chart as the earlier equality proof, lambda3=(1,0), \
lambda4=(0,1), lambda5=(1,1), so Z_ref=zeta3 zeta4 zeta5=alpha beta(alpha-beta). Let D=A3 A4 A5 B3 \
B4 B5 and N_H=[45]^2 K3 B4 B5+[35]^2 K4 B3 B5+[34]^2 K5 B3 B4.", "Text"], 
   Cell["Define V_i=<Xi|p1|i] and W_i=<Xi|p2|i]. The positive numerator is N_common=Sum[V_a (W_b+zeta_c[cb]) W_c A_b A_c B_a B_b, all six orders]. The minus signs in P_abc and the diagram prefactor cancel, so M_raw_common=2 Sqrt[2] EE^3 <bold1 bold2> N_common/(Me Z_ref D).", "Text"],
   Cell["After clearing D and Z_ref, the raw common-reference numerator obeys N_common=Me^2 Z_ref \
N_H using only the external equal-mass condition E=det(p2)-det(p1)=0 and conservation. \
Equivalently, its alpha^3 and beta^3 coefficients vanish, its alpha^2 beta coefficient is Me^2 N_H, \
and its alpha beta^2 coefficient is -Me^2 N_H. The exact four coefficient checks below prove the \
entire reference polynomial cancels. This manipulates the cleared polynomial; it does not evaluate \
singular reference choices in individual diagrams.", "Text"], Cell["Independently, the exact \
retained remainders satisfy Sum[R_abc/(A_a B_c), all six orders]=0 for this common reference. The \
unreduced common-reference sum and the sum of the scoped numerator reductions are therefore the \
same off-shell rational expression. No internal condition is imposed on the combined sum. In \
contrast, dropping only part of a diagram's cut remainder need not preserve this cancellation.", 
    "Text"], Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Generic Exact Algebra", "Subsection"], 
      Cell["ClearAll[q5VerifyCommonReference];\nq5VerifyCommonReference[] := Module[{j, l, adj, \
lam, til, pm, an, sq, yy,\n    aa, bb, kc, rho, zeta, vxi, wxi, vars, ext, reduce, orders, nh, \
nc,\n    zref, mass2, difference, factorCoefficients, localChecks, remainderNumerator,\n    \
cyclicNumerator, localRemainder, cutVars, cutBasis, cutChecks,\n    alpha, beta, u, v, w, z, r, s, \
t},\n  j = {{0, -1}, {1, 0}}; l = -j;\n  adj[p_] := {{p[[2, 2]], -p[[1, 2]]}, {-p[[2, 1]], p[[1, \
1]]}};\n  lam[3] = {1, 0}; lam[4] = {0, 1}; lam[5] = {1, 1};\n  til[3] = {1, 0}; til[4] = {0, r}; \
til[5] = {s, t};\n  pm[1] = {{u, v}, {w, z}};\n  Do[pm[i] = Outer[Times, lam[i], til[i]], {i, 3, \
5}];\n  pm[2] = -pm[1] - Total[pm /@ {3, 4, 5}];\n  an[a_, b_] := lam[a].j.lam[b];\n  sq[a_, b_] := \
til[a].l.til[b];\n  yy[a_, p_, b_] := lam[a].j.pm[p].l.til[b];\n  aa[i_] := Expand[Det[pm[1] + \
pm[i]] - Det[pm[1]]];\n  bb[i_] := Expand[Det[pm[2] + pm[i]] - Det[pm[2]]];\n  kc[i_] := \
til[i].adj[pm[1]].pm[2].l.til[i];\n  rho = {alpha, beta};\n  zeta[i_] := rho.j.lam[i];\n  vxi[i_] \
:= rho.j.pm[1].l.til[i];\n  wxi[i_] := rho.j.pm[2].l.til[i];\n  vars = {z, w, v, u, t, s, r, beta, \
alpha};\n  ext = Expand[Det[pm[2]] - Det[pm[1]]];\n  mass2 = Det[pm[1]];\n  reduce[p_] := \
Last[PolynomialReduce[Expand[p], {ext}, vars]];\n  orders = Permutations[{3, 4, 5}];\n  nh = \
Expand[Total[Function[c, With[{ab = Complement[{3, 4, 5}, {c}]},\n    (sq @@ ab)^2 kc[c] Times @@ \
(bb /@ ab)]] /@ {3, 4, 5}]];\n  nc = Expand[Total[Function[ord, With[{a = ord[[1]], b = ord[[2]], c \
= ord[[3]]},\n    vxi[a] (wxi[b] + zeta[c] sq[c, b]) wxi[c] *\n      aa[b] aa[c] bb[a] bb[b]]] /@ \
orders]];\n  zref = Times @@ (zeta /@ {3, 4, 5});\n  difference = reduce[nc - mass2 zref nh];\n  \
factorCoefficients = Table[\n    reduce[Coefficient[Coefficient[nc - mass2 zref nh, alpha, k], \
beta, 3 - k]] === 0,\n    {k, 0, 3}];\n  localChecks = Function[ord, With[{a = ord[[1]], b = \
ord[[2]], c = ord[[3]]},\n    Module[{f, f0, delta, numerator, product, target, remainder},\n      \
f = {-vxi[a]/zeta[a],\n        (wxi[b] + zeta[c] sq[c, b])/zeta[b], wxi[c]/zeta[c]};\n      f0 = \
{yy[b, 1, a]/an[a, b], -yy[a, 1, b]/an[a, b], yy[a, 2, c]/an[a, c]};\n      delta = {-zeta[b] \
aa[a]/(an[a, b] zeta[a]),\n        zeta[a] (bb[c] - aa[a])/(an[a, b] zeta[b]),\n        -zeta[a] \
bb[c]/(an[a, c] zeta[c])};\n      numerator[x_] := Numerator[Together[x]];\n      product = Times \
@@ f;\n      target = -mass2 sq[a, b] yy[a, 2, c]/(an[a, b] an[a, c]);\n      remainder = \
delta[[1]] f[[2]] f[[3]] + f0[[1]] delta[[2]] f[[3]] +\n        f0[[1]] f0[[2]] delta[[3]] - aa[a] \
aa[b] yy[a, 2, c]/(an[a, b]^2 an[a, c]);\n      <|\"Order\" -> ord,\n        \
\"ThreeReferenceIdentities\" -> (reduce[numerator[#]] === 0 & /@ (f - f0 - delta)),\n        \
\"DeterminantSchouten\" -> (reduce[yy[b, 1, a] yy[a, 1, b] -\n          mass2 an[a, b] sq[a, b] - \
aa[a] aa[b]] === 0),\n        \"ExactRemainderIdentity\" -> (reduce[numerator[product - target - \
remainder]] === 0)|>\n    ]]] /@ orders;\n  cyclicNumerator = Together[Total[Function[ord,\n    \
With[{a = ord[[1]], b = ord[[2]], c = ord[[3]]},\n      -mass2 sq[a, b] yy[a, 2, c]/(an[a, b] an[a, \
c] aa[a] bb[c])]] /@ orders] *\n      Times @@ Join[aa /@ {3, 4, 5}, bb /@ {3, 4, 5}]];\n  \
remainderNumerator = reduce[-nc - zref cyclicNumerator];\n  <|\"ExternalEqualMassCondition\" -> \
ext,\n    \"ReferenceComponents\" -> {alpha, beta},\n    \"ReferenceDenominator\" -> zref,\n    \
\"FourReferenceCoefficientChecks\" -> factorCoefficients,\n    \"SixDiagramIdentityChecks\" -> \
localChecks,\n    \"RetainedRemaindersCancelInFullSum\" -> (remainderNumerator === 0),\n    \
\"RawCommonSumEqualsThreeTermH\" -> (difference === 0),\n    \
\"CommonEqualsCyclicIncludingNormalization\" -> (difference === 0),\n    \
\"CommonEqualsHalfMomentumReferenceResult\" -> (difference === 0),\n    \
\"InternalConditionsInGlobalSumProof\" -> None|>\n];\nq5CommonProof = \
q5VerifyCommonReference[];\nKeyTake[q5CommonProof, {\"FourReferenceCoefficientChecks\", \
\"RetainedRemaindersCancelInFullSum\", \"RawCommonSumEqualsThreeTermH\", \
\"CommonEqualsCyclicIncludingNormalization\", \"CommonEqualsHalfMomentumReferenceResult\", \
\"InternalConditionsInGlobalSumProof\"}]", "Input"], 
      Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"", RowBox[{RowBox[{"\"FourReferenceCoefficientChecks\"", "", 
              RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"True", ",", "True", ",", "True", ",", "True"}], "}"}]}], ",", 
            RowBox[{"\"RetainedRemaindersCancelInFullSum\"", "", "True"}], ",", 
            RowBox[{"\"RawCommonSumEqualsThreeTermH\"", "", "True"}], ",", 
            RowBox[{"\"CommonEqualsCyclicIncludingNormalization\"", "", "True"}], ",", 
            RowBox[{"\"CommonEqualsHalfMomentumReferenceResult\"", "", "True"}], ",", 
            RowBox[{"\"InternalConditionsInGlobalSumProof\"", "", "None"}]}], ""}]], 
       "Output"]}, Closed]], Cell["Compact Result", "Subsection"], 
   Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["q5CommonSpin = SpinorChain[Spinor[\"Spin\", \"Angle\", 1], \
Spinor[\"Spin\", \"Angle\", 2]];\nq5CommonFinal = 2 Sqrt[2] EE^3 Me q5CommonSpin/(q5A[3] q5A[4] \
q5A[5]) *\n  (q5Square[4, 5]^2 q5K[3]/q5B[3] + q5Square[3, 5]^2 q5K[4]/q5B[4] +\n    q5Square[3, \
4]^2 q5K[5]/q5B[5]);\nq5CommonFinal", "Input"], 
      Cell[BoxData[FractionBox[RowBox[{"2", " ", SqrtBox["2"], " ", SuperscriptBox["EE", "3"], " ", 
           "Me", " ", TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"〈\"", StyleBox["1", Bold, StripOnInput -> 
                 False]}, "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[{StyleBox["2", Bold, StripOnInput -> False], 
               "\"〉\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"], " ", 
           RowBox[{"(", RowBox[{FractionBox[RowBox[{SuperscriptBox[TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[
                      {"\"[\"", "4"}, "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[{"5", "\"]\""}, "RowDefault"]}, 
                    "RowDefault"], "2"], " ", TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"[\"", "3"}, 
                     "RowDefault"], "\"|\"", SubscriptBox["p", "1"], SubscriptBox["p", "2"], 
                    "\"|\"", TemplateBox[{"3", "\"]\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"]}], 
                RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], "+", SubsuperscriptBox["p", 
                   RowBox[{"2", ",", "3"}], "2"]}]], "+", FractionBox[RowBox[{SuperscriptBox[
                   TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"[\"", "3"}, "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[
                      {"5", "\"]\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"], "2"], " ", TemplateBox[
                   {TemplateBox[{"\"[\"", "4"}, "RowDefault"], "\"|\"", SubscriptBox["p", "1"], 
                    SubscriptBox["p", "2"], "\"|\"", TemplateBox[{"4", "\"]\""}, "RowDefault"]}, 
                   "RowDefault"]}], RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], "+", 
                  SubsuperscriptBox["p", RowBox[{"2", ",", "4"}], "2"]}]], "+", FractionBox[
                RowBox[{SuperscriptBox[TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"[\"", "3"}, "RowDefault"], 
                     TemplateBox[{"4", "\"]\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"], "2"], " ", 
                  TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"[\"", "5"}, "RowDefault"], "\"|\"", SubscriptBox[
                     "p", "1"], SubscriptBox["p", "2"], "\"|\"", TemplateBox[{"5", "\"]\""}, 
                     "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"]}], RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", 
                     "2"]}], "+", SubsuperscriptBox["p", RowBox[{"2", ",", "5"}], "2"]}]]}], 
             ")"}]}], RowBox[{RowBox[{"(", RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], "+", 
               SubsuperscriptBox["p", RowBox[{"1", ",", "3"}], "2"]}], ")"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"(", RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], "+", SubsuperscriptBox[
                "p", RowBox[{"1", ",", "4"}], "2"]}], ")"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"(", RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], "+", SubsuperscriptBox[
                "p", RowBox[{"1", ",", "5"}], "2"]}], ")"}]}]]], "Output"]}, Open]], 
   Cell["The common reference cancels completely. The final result has the same three physical-pole \
terms as q5CyclicFinal, including its coefficient, and is q5Final/2. No rescaling is used. This is \
a simpler reference-cancellation derivation, but no genuinely shorter final rational form was \
found. Combining the three terms with Together produces a larger numerator rather than a useful \
simplification.", "Text"], Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["<|\"RawCommonReferenceProof\" -> \
q5CommonProof[\"RawCommonSumEqualsThreeTermH\"],\n  \"CommonEqualsCyclic\" -> \
(Together[q5CommonFinal - q5CyclicFinal] === 0),\n  \"TwiceCommonEqualsMomentumReference\" -> \
(Together[2 q5CommonFinal - q5Final] === 0)|>", "Input"], 
      Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"", RowBox[{RowBox[{"\"RawCommonReferenceProof\"", "", "True"}], 
            ",", RowBox[{"\"CommonEqualsCyclic\"", "", "True"}], ",", 
            RowBox[{"\"TwiceCommonEqualsMomentumReference\"", "", "True"}]}], ""}]], 
       "Output"]}, Open]], Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Checks Against The Generated Diagrams", 
       "Subsection"], Cell["The checks below use the actual diagramAmplitudes output. There are 72 \
exact per-diagram double-cut checks (six orders, four masses, three regular common references) with \
original PropDen factors kept opaque, plus 12 exact full-sum checks on external-shell kinematics \
with every original propagator nonzero. These checks validate the common-reference calculation; \
they are not an independent Feynman normalization calculation.", "Text"], 
      Cell["ClearAll[q5CheckCommonGeneratedDiagrams];\nq5CheckCommonGeneratedDiagrams[amps_List] := \
Module[{jj, kk, adj, outer, perp, pl, angle, square, mixed,\n    angleEndpoint, rawEval, reference, \
lam, til, Den, checks, raw, order, a, b, c, mass,\n    q1, q2, den, reduced, actual, zeta, vxi, \
wxi, formula, uncutChecks,\n    q5SampleR, q5SampleS, q5SampleU, q5SampleV, q5SampleW, q5SampleZ, \
q5SampleT,\n    av, bv, kin, h, denRules, sum, summary},\njj = {{0, -1}, {1, 0}}; kk = \
-jj;\nadj[p_] := {{p[[2, 2]], -p[[1, 2]]}, {-p[[2, 1]], p[[1, 1]]}};\nouter[u_, v_] := Outer[Times, \
u, v];\nperp[u_] := {-u[[2]], u[[1]]};\npl[Multiparticle[x__]] := Total[pl /@ {x}];\nangle[a_, b_] \
:= lam[a].jj.lam[b];\nsquare[a_, b_] := til[a].kk.til[b];\nmixed[a_, p_, b_] := \
lam[a].jj.pl[p].kk.til[b];\nangleEndpoint[Spinor[\"Xi\", \"Angle\", _]] := \
reference;\nangleEndpoint[Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Angle\", i_]] := lam[i];\nrawEval[expr_] := expr \
/. {\n  PropDen[p_, mass_] :> Den[p, mass],\n  SpinorChain[Spinor[\"Spin\", \"Angle\", 1], \
Spinor[\"Spin\", \"Angle\", 2]] -> 1,\n  SpinorChain[x : Spinor[_, \"Angle\", _], Mom[p_], \
Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Square\", i_]] :>\n    angleEndpoint[x].jj.pl[p].kk.til[i],\n  SpinorChain[x \
: Spinor[_, \"Angle\", _], Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Angle\", i_]] :>\n    \
angleEndpoint[x].jj.lam[i]};\nchecks = {};\nDo[\n  raw = ReduceSpinContractions[amps[[index, 2]]] \
/. amps[[index, 1]];\n  order = Table[First[Cases[raw,\n    SpinorChain[Spinor[\"Xi\", \"Angle\", 9 \
+ n], Mom[_], Spinor[\"Helicity\", \"Square\", photon_]] :> photon,\n    Infinity]], {n, 3}];\n  \
{a, b, c} = order;\n  Do[\n    mass = sample;\n    lam[3] = {1, sample + 1}; lam[4] = {sample + 2, \
1}; lam[5] = {2, 2 sample + 3};\n    pl[1] = {{sample + 1, sample - 2}, {sample + 2,\n      (mass^2 \
+ (sample - 2) (sample + 2))/(sample + 1)}};\n    til[a] = (sample + 2) perp[adj[pl[1]].lam[a]];\n  \
  pl[a] = outer[lam[a], til[a]];\n    q1 = pl[1] + pl[a];\n    til[b] = (sample - 5) \
perp[adj[q1].lam[b]];\n    pl[b] = outer[lam[b], til[b]];\n    q2 = -q1 - pl[b];\n    til[c] = \
(sample + 3) perp[adj[q2].lam[c]];\n    pl[c] = outer[lam[c], til[c]];\n    pl[2] = q2 - pl[c];\n   \
 den = Times @@ DeleteDuplicates[Cases[raw, _PropDen, Infinity]];\n    reduced = 2 Sqrt[2] mass \
square[a, b] mixed[a, 2, c]/\n      (angle[a, b] angle[a, c] den) /. PropDen -> Den /. Me -> \
mass;\n    Do[\n      reference = vector;\n      actual = rawEval[raw /. {Me -> mass, EE -> 1}];\n  \
    zeta[i_] := reference.jj.lam[i];\n      vxi[i_] := reference.jj.pl[1].kk.til[i];\n      wxi[i_] \
:= reference.jj.pl[2].kk.til[i];\n      formula = 2 Sqrt[2]/mass * vxi[a] (wxi[b] + zeta[c] \
square[c, b]) wxi[c]/\n        (zeta[a] zeta[b] zeta[c] den) /. PropDen -> Den /. Me -> mass;\n     \
 AppendTo[checks, <|\"Order\" -> order, \"Mass\" -> mass, \"Reference\" -> reference,\n        \
\"Shells\" -> ({Det[pl[1]], Det[pl[2]], Det[q1], Det[q2]} === ConstantArray[mass^2, 4]),\n        \
\"RegularReference\" -> AllTrue[zeta /@ {3, 4, 5}, # != 0 &],\n        \"RawFormula\" -> \
(Together[actual - formula] === 0),\n        \"OnCutReducedDiagram\" -> (Together[actual - reduced] \
=== 0)|>],\n      {vector, {{17, 29}, {31, 43}, {47, 53}}}],\n    {sample, 1, 4}], {index, \
6}];\nuncutChecks = {};\nDo[\n  mass = sample;\n  lam[3] = {1, 0}; lam[4] = {0, 1}; lam[5] = {1, \
1};\n  q5SampleR = sample + 3; q5SampleS = sample + 1; q5SampleU = sample + 2;\n  q5SampleV = \
sample - 3; q5SampleW = sample + 1;\n  q5SampleZ = (mass^2 + q5SampleV q5SampleW)/q5SampleU;\n  \
q5SampleT = -(q5SampleR (1 + q5SampleS + q5SampleU) +\n    q5SampleS (q5SampleZ - q5SampleV) + \
q5SampleZ)/(1 + q5SampleU - q5SampleW);\n  til[3] = {1, 0}; til[4] = {0, q5SampleR}; til[5] = \
{q5SampleS, q5SampleT};\n  pl[1] = {{q5SampleU, q5SampleV}, {q5SampleW, q5SampleZ}};\n  Do[pl[i] = \
outer[lam[i], til[i]], {i, 3, 5}];\n  pl[2] = -pl[1] - Total[pl /@ {3, 4, 5}];\n  av[i_] := \
Det[pl[1] + pl[i]] - mass^2;\n  bv[i_] := Det[pl[2] + pl[i]] - mass^2;\n  kin[i_] := \
til[i].adj[pl[1]].pl[2].kk.til[i];\n  h = Total[Function[c, With[{ab = Complement[{3, 4, 5}, \
{c}]},\n    (square @@ ab)^2 kin[c]/bv[c]]] /@ {3, 4, 5}]/(av[3] av[4] av[5]);\n  denRules = \
Den[Mom[Multiparticle[x__]], Me] :> Det[Total[pl /@ {x}]] - mass^2;\n  Do[\n    reference = \
vector;\n    sum = Total[rawEval[ReduceSpinContractions[#[[2]]] /. #[[1]] /. EE -> 1] & /@ amps] \
/.\n      denRules /. Me -> mass;\n    AppendTo[uncutChecks, <|\"Mass\" -> mass, \"Reference\" -> \
reference,\n      \"ExternalShells\" -> ({Det[pl[1]], Det[pl[2]]} === {mass^2, mass^2}),\n      \
\"AllOriginalPropagatorsNonzero\" -> AllTrue[Join[av /@ {3, 4, 5}, bv /@ {3, 4, 5}], # != 0 &],\n   \
   \"RawSumEqualsCompactResult\" -> (Together[sum - 2 Sqrt[2] mass h] === 0)|>],\n    {vector, \
{{17, 29}, {31, 43}, {47, 53}}}], {sample, 1, 4}];\nsummary = <|\"ExactCutChecks\" -> \
Length[checks], \"ExactUncutSumChecks\" -> Length[uncutChecks],\n  \"AllPass\" -> AllTrue[checks, \
#[\"Shells\"] && #[\"RegularReference\"] &&\n    #[\"RawFormula\"] && #[\"OnCutReducedDiagram\"] &] \
&&\n    AllTrue[uncutChecks, #[\"ExternalShells\"] && #[\"AllOriginalPropagatorsNonzero\"] &&\n     \
 #[\"RawSumEqualsCompactResult\"] &], \"Details\" -> checks, \"UncutDetails\" -> \
uncutChecks|>;\n\nsummary\n];\nq5CommonActualChecks = \
q5CheckCommonGeneratedDiagrams[q5CommonInput];\nKeyTake[q5CommonActualChecks, {\"ExactCutChecks\", \
\"ExactUncutSumChecks\", \"AllPass\"}]", "Input"], 
      Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"", RowBox[{RowBox[{"\"ExactCutChecks\"", "", "72"}], ",", 
            RowBox[{"\"ExactUncutSumChecks\"", "", "12"}], ",", 
            RowBox[{"\"AllPass\"", "", "True"}]}], ""}]], "Output"]}, Closed]]}, Open]]
,
Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Mixed Helicity: e, E, A.+, A.+, A.-", "Section"], 
   Cell["All momenta are ingoing. Photons 3 and 4 have positive helicity; photon 5 has negative \
helicity. This section preserves the earlier all-plus results. The compact physical QED amplitude \
below is not identical to the arbitrary-reference raw constructive sum: that sum has a \
reference-dependent off-shell continuation in this helicity sector. We retain the on-shell \
numerator residues, keep every original PropDen off shell, and fix the full completion \
independently with ordinary QED diagrams.", "Text"], 
   Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Generate The Six Mixed Diagrams", "Subsection"], 
      Cell["q5MixedModel = ReadModel[FileNameJoin[{DirectoryName[$HEPCATpath], \"models\"}], \
1];\nq5MixedDiagrams = CreateDiagrams[\"e\", \"E\", \"A.+\", \"A.+\", \"A.-\", \
q5MixedModel];\nq5MixedInput = diagramAmplitudes[q5MixedDiagrams];\nq5MixedRaw = \
(ReduceSpinContractions[Last[#]] /. First[#] &) /@ q5MixedInput;\n<|\"DiagramCount\" -> \
Length[q5MixedRaw], \"RawLeafCounts\" -> (LeafCount /@ q5MixedRaw)|>", "Input"], 
      Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"", RowBox[{RowBox[{"\"DiagramCount\"", "", "6"}], ",", 
            RowBox[{"\"RawLeafCounts\"", "", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"114", ",", "118", ",", "114", 
                  ",", "118", ",", "114", ",", "114"}], "}"}]}]}], ""}]], "Output"]}, Closed]], 
   Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Definitions And Both Final Forms", "Subsection"], 
      Cell["U=<bold1 bold2>, V=<bold1 5><bold2 5>, Fi=<5|p1|i], Gi=<5|p2|i], Ki=[i|p1 p2|i], \
L=<5|p1 p2|5>, Ai=(p1+ki)^2-Me^2, Bi=(p2+ki)^2-Me^2. All six Ai,Bi remain off-shell propagators. \
The spurious formula uses Gamma=<53><54>, Dij=[i|p1(ki+k5)|j], Cij=1+Ai/A5+Bj/B5, and S=(p1+p2)^2. \
The two ordered pairs are (3,4) and (4,3).", "Text"], Cell["ClearAll[q5MPSpinor, q5MPAngle, \
q5MPSquare, q5MPF, q5MPG, q5MPK,\n  q5MPL, q5MPA, q5MPB, q5MPD, q5MPC, q5MPS, q5MPGap,\n  q5MPU, \
q5MPV, q5MPSeed, q5MPCompletion, q5MixedSpurious,\n  q5MixedFinal, \
q5MPPhysicalDenominators];\nq5MPSpinor[i_, chirality_] := Spinor[If[MemberQ[{1, 2}, i], \"Spin\", \
\"Helicity\"], chirality, i];\nq5MPAngle[i_, j_] := SpinorChain[q5MPSpinor[i, \"Angle\"], \
q5MPSpinor[j, \"Angle\"]];\nq5MPSquare[i_, j_] := SpinorChain[q5MPSpinor[i, \"Square\"], \
q5MPSpinor[j, \"Square\"]];\nq5MPF[i_] := SpinorChain[q5MPSpinor[5, \"Angle\"], Mom[1], \
q5MPSpinor[i, \"Square\"]];\nq5MPG[i_] := SpinorChain[q5MPSpinor[5, \"Angle\"], Mom[2], \
q5MPSpinor[i, \"Square\"]];\nq5MPK[i_] := SpinorChain[q5MPSpinor[i, \"Square\"], Mom[1], Mom[2], \
q5MPSpinor[i, \"Square\"]];\nq5MPL = SpinorChain[q5MPSpinor[5, \"Angle\"], Mom[1], Mom[2], \
q5MPSpinor[5, \"Angle\"]];\nq5MPA[i_] := PropDen[Mom[Multiparticle[1, i]], Me];\nq5MPB[i_] := \
PropDen[Mom[Multiparticle[2, i]], Me];\nq5MPD[i_, j_] := SpinorChain[q5MPSpinor[i, \"Square\"], \
Mom[1],\n  Mom[Multiparticle[i, 5]], q5MPSpinor[j, \"Square\"]];\nq5MPC[i_, j_] := 1 + \
q5MPA[i]/q5MPA[5] + q5MPB[j]/q5MPB[5];\nq5MPS = 2 (MomProd[3, 4] + MomProd[3, 5] + MomProd[4, \
5]);\nq5MPGap = q5MPAngle[5, 3] q5MPAngle[5, 4];\nq5MPU = q5MPAngle[1, 2];\nq5MPV = q5MPAngle[1, 5] \
q5MPAngle[2, 5];\nq5MPSeed = 2 Sqrt[2] EE^3/Me Total[Function[ord,\n    With[{i = ord[[1]], j = \
ord[[2]]},\n      q5MPC[i, j] q5MPF[i] q5MPG[j]/(q5MPA[i] q5MPB[j] q5MPGap) *\n        (q5MPV - \
q5MPU q5MPF[i] q5MPG[j]/q5MPD[i, j])]] /@ {{3, 4}, {4, 3}}];\nq5MPCompletion = -2 Sqrt[2] EE^3 Me \
q5MPU Total[Function[ord,\n    With[{i = ord[[1]], j = ord[[2]]},\n      q5MPC[i, j] q5MPSquare[i, \
j]^4/\n        (q5MPS q5MPSquare[i, 5] q5MPSquare[5, j] q5MPD[i, j])]] /@ {{3, 4}, {4, \
3}}];\nq5MixedSpurious = q5MPSeed + q5MPCompletion;\nq5MixedFinal = 2 Sqrt[2] EE^3/(Me q5MPA[3] \
q5MPA[4] q5MPA[5]) *\n  (q5MPF[3] q5MPK[4] (q5MPU q5MPF[3] - q5MPV q5MPSquare[3, 5])/q5MPB[4] +\n   \
q5MPF[4] q5MPK[3] (q5MPU q5MPF[4] - q5MPV q5MPSquare[4, 5])/q5MPB[3] +\n   Me^2 q5MPSquare[3, 4]^2 \
(q5MPU q5MPL + q5MPV (q5MPA[5] + q5MPB[5]))/q5MPB[5]);\nq5MPPhysicalDenominators = Join[q5MPA /@ \
{3, 4, 5}, q5MPB /@ {3, 4, 5}];", "Input"]}, Closed]], Cell["Three Terms With Physical Poles Only", 
    "Subsection"], Cell["q5MixedFinal is the most compact form found: three additive terms, \
manifest 3<->4 Bose symmetry, and no reference-spinor or photon-collinear denominator factors. \
There is no claim that three terms is an absolute minimum. Me is nonzero; no massless \
charged-particle limit is taken.", "Text"], 
   Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["q5MixedFinal", "Input"], 
      Cell[BoxData[FractionBox[RowBox[{"2", " ", SqrtBox["2"], " ", SuperscriptBox["EE", "3"], " ", 
           RowBox[{"(", RowBox[{FractionBox[RowBox[{SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"], " ", SuperscriptBox[
                   TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"[\"", "3"}, "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[
                      {"4", "\"]\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"], "2"], " ", RowBox[
                   {"(", RowBox[{RowBox[{RowBox[{"(", RowBox[{RowBox[{"(", RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", 
                                 SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], "+", SubsuperscriptBox["p", RowBox[
                                 {"1", ",", "5"}], "2"]}], ")"}], "+", RowBox[{"(", RowBox[
                               {RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], "+", SubsuperscriptBox[
                                 "p", RowBox[{"2", ",", "5"}], "2"]}], ")"}]}], ")"}], " ", 
                        TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"〈\"", StyleBox["1", Bold, StripOnInput -> 
                              False]}, "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[{"5", "\"〉\""}, "RowDefault"]}, 
                         "RowDefault"], " ", TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"〈\"", StyleBox["2", 
                             Bold, StripOnInput -> False]}, "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[{"5", 
                            "\"〉\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"]}], "+", RowBox[
                       {TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"〈\"", StyleBox["1", Bold, StripOnInput -> 
                              False]}, "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[{StyleBox["2", Bold, 
                             StripOnInput -> False], "\"〉\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"], 
                        " ", TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"〈\"", "5"}, "RowDefault"], "\"|\"", 
                          SubscriptBox["p", "1"], SubscriptBox["p", "2"], "\"|\"", TemplateBox[
                           {"5", "\"〉\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"]}]}], ")"}]}], 
                RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], "+", SubsuperscriptBox["p", 
                   RowBox[{"2", ",", "5"}], "2"]}]], "+", FractionBox[RowBox[
                 {TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"〈\"", "5"}, "RowDefault"], "\"|\"", SubscriptBox[
                     "p", "1"], "\"|\"", TemplateBox[{"4", "\"]\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"], 
                  " ", RowBox[{"(", RowBox[{RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"[\"", 
                              "4"}, "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[{"5", "\"]\""}, "RowDefault"]}, 
                           "RowDefault"]}], " ", TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"〈\"", StyleBox["1", 
                             Bold, StripOnInput -> False]}, "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[{"5", 
                            "\"〉\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"], " ", TemplateBox[
                         {TemplateBox[{"\"〈\"", StyleBox["2", Bold, StripOnInput -> False]}, 
                           "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[{"5", "\"〉\""}, "RowDefault"]}, 
                         "RowDefault"]}], "+", RowBox[{TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"〈\"", 
                            StyleBox["1", Bold, StripOnInput -> False]}, "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[
                           {StyleBox["2", Bold, StripOnInput -> False], "\"〉\""}, "RowDefault"]}, 
                         "RowDefault"], " ", TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"〈\"", "5"}, 
                           "RowDefault"], "\"|\"", SubscriptBox["p", "1"], "\"|\"", TemplateBox[
                           {"4", "\"]\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"]}]}], ")"}], " ", 
                  TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"[\"", "3"}, "RowDefault"], "\"|\"", SubscriptBox[
                     "p", "1"], SubscriptBox["p", "2"], "\"|\"", TemplateBox[{"3", "\"]\""}, 
                     "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"]}], RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", 
                     "2"]}], "+", SubsuperscriptBox["p", RowBox[{"2", ",", "3"}], "2"]}]], "+", 
               FractionBox[RowBox[{TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"〈\"", "5"}, "RowDefault"], 
                    "\"|\"", SubscriptBox["p", "1"], "\"|\"", TemplateBox[{"3", "\"]\""}, 
                     "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"], " ", RowBox[{"(", RowBox[
                     {RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"[\"", "3"}, "RowDefault"], 
                            TemplateBox[{"5", "\"]\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"]}], " ", 
                        TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"〈\"", StyleBox["1", Bold, StripOnInput -> 
                              False]}, "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[{"5", "\"〉\""}, "RowDefault"]}, 
                         "RowDefault"], " ", TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"〈\"", StyleBox["2", 
                             Bold, StripOnInput -> False]}, "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[{"5", 
                            "\"〉\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"]}], "+", RowBox[
                       {TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"〈\"", StyleBox["1", Bold, StripOnInput -> 
                              False]}, "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[{StyleBox["2", Bold, 
                             StripOnInput -> False], "\"〉\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"], 
                        " ", TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"〈\"", "5"}, "RowDefault"], "\"|\"", 
                          SubscriptBox["p", "1"], "\"|\"", TemplateBox[{"3", "\"]\""}, 
                           "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"]}]}], ")"}], " ", TemplateBox[
                   {TemplateBox[{"\"[\"", "4"}, "RowDefault"], "\"|\"", SubscriptBox["p", "1"], 
                    SubscriptBox["p", "2"], "\"|\"", TemplateBox[{"4", "\"]\""}, "RowDefault"]}, 
                   "RowDefault"]}], RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], "+", 
                  SubsuperscriptBox["p", RowBox[{"2", ",", "4"}], "2"]}]]}], ")"}]}], 
         RowBox[{"Me", " ", RowBox[{"(", RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], "+", 
               SubsuperscriptBox["p", RowBox[{"1", ",", "3"}], "2"]}], ")"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"(", RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], "+", SubsuperscriptBox[
                "p", RowBox[{"1", ",", "4"}], "2"]}], ")"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"(", RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], "+", SubsuperscriptBox[
                "p", RowBox[{"1", ",", "5"}], "2"]}], ")"}]}]]], "Output"]}, Open]], 
   Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Equivalent Form With Spurious Poles", "Subsection"], 
      Cell["q5MPSeed is residue compatible but incomplete. q5MPCompletion is the cut-invisible U \
correction needed by the physical amplitude. q5MixedSpurious is their sum. Its apparent Dij, S, \
angle-reference, and square-bracket poles cancel exactly. This is not a factor-of-two relation.", 
       "Text"], Cell["q5MixedSpurious", "Input"], 
      Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{FractionBox[RowBox[{"2", " ", SqrtBox["2"], " ", SuperscriptBox["EE", 
              "3"], " ", RowBox[{"(", RowBox[{FractionBox[RowBox[{RowBox[{"(", RowBox[{"1", "+", 
                        FractionBox[RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], "+", 
                           SubsuperscriptBox["p", RowBox[{"1", ",", "3"}], "2"]}], RowBox[
                          {RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], "+", SubsuperscriptBox["p", 
                            RowBox[{"1", ",", "5"}], "2"]}]], "+", FractionBox[RowBox[
                          {RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], "+", SubsuperscriptBox["p", 
                            RowBox[{"2", ",", "4"}], "2"]}], RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox[
                              "Me", "2"]}], "+", SubsuperscriptBox["p", RowBox[{"2", ",", "5"}], 
                            "2"]}]]}], ")"}], " ", TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"〈\"", "5"}, 
                       "RowDefault"], "\"|\"", SubscriptBox["p", "1"], "\"|\"", TemplateBox[
                       {"3", "\"]\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"], " ", TemplateBox[
                     {TemplateBox[{"\"〈\"", "5"}, "RowDefault"], "\"|\"", SubscriptBox["p", "2"], 
                      "\"|\"", TemplateBox[{"4", "\"]\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"], " ", 
                    RowBox[{"(", RowBox[{RowBox[{TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"〈\"", StyleBox["1", 
                               Bold, StripOnInput -> False]}, "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[{"5", 
                              "\"〉\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"], " ", TemplateBox[
                           {TemplateBox[{"\"〈\"", StyleBox["2", Bold, StripOnInput -> False]}, 
                             "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[{"5", "\"〉\""}, "RowDefault"]}, 
                           "RowDefault"]}], "-", FractionBox[RowBox[{TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[
                              {"\"〈\"", StyleBox["1", Bold, StripOnInput -> False]}, 
                              "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[{StyleBox["2", Bold, StripOnInput -> 
                                 False], "\"〉\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"], " ", 
                           TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"〈\"", "5"}, "RowDefault"], "\"|\"", 
                             SubscriptBox["p", "1"], "\"|\"", TemplateBox[{"3", "\"]\""}, 
                              "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"], " ", TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[
                              {"\"〈\"", "5"}, "RowDefault"], "\"|\"", SubscriptBox["p", "2"], 
                             "\"|\"", TemplateBox[{"4", "\"]\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"]}], 
                         TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"[\"", "3"}, "RowDefault"], "\"|\"", 
                           SubscriptBox["p", "1"], SubscriptBox["p", RowBox[{"3", ",", "5"}]], 
                           "\"|\"", TemplateBox[{"4", "\"]\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"]]}], 
                      ")"}]}], RowBox[{RowBox[{"(", RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", 
                           "2"]}], "+", SubsuperscriptBox["p", RowBox[{"1", ",", "3"}], "2"]}], 
                      ")"}], " ", RowBox[{"(", RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], 
                        "+", SubsuperscriptBox["p", RowBox[{"2", ",", "4"}], "2"]}], ")"}], " ", 
                    TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"〈\"", "5"}, "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[
                       {"3", "\"〉\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"], " ", TemplateBox[
                     {TemplateBox[{"\"〈\"", "5"}, "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[{"4", "\"〉\""}, 
                       "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"]}]], "+", FractionBox[RowBox[
                   {RowBox[{"(", RowBox[{"1", "+", FractionBox[RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox[
                              "Me", "2"]}], "+", SubsuperscriptBox["p", RowBox[{"1", ",", "4"}], 
                            "2"]}], RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], "+", 
                           SubsuperscriptBox["p", RowBox[{"1", ",", "5"}], "2"]}]], "+", 
                        FractionBox[RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], "+", 
                           SubsuperscriptBox["p", RowBox[{"2", ",", "3"}], "2"]}], RowBox[
                          {RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], "+", SubsuperscriptBox["p", 
                            RowBox[{"2", ",", "5"}], "2"]}]]}], ")"}], " ", TemplateBox[
                     {TemplateBox[{"\"〈\"", "5"}, "RowDefault"], "\"|\"", SubscriptBox["p", "1"], 
                      "\"|\"", TemplateBox[{"4", "\"]\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"], " ", 
                    TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"〈\"", "5"}, "RowDefault"], "\"|\"", SubscriptBox[
                       "p", "2"], "\"|\"", TemplateBox[{"3", "\"]\""}, "RowDefault"]}, 
                     "RowDefault"], " ", RowBox[{"(", RowBox[{RowBox[{TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[
                             {"\"〈\"", StyleBox["1", Bold, StripOnInput -> False]}, 
                             "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[{"5", "\"〉\""}, "RowDefault"]}, 
                           "RowDefault"], " ", TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"〈\"", StyleBox["2", 
                               Bold, StripOnInput -> False]}, "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[{"5", 
                              "\"〉\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"]}], "-", FractionBox[
                         RowBox[{TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"〈\"", StyleBox["1", Bold, 
                                StripOnInput -> False]}, "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[{StyleBox["2", 
                                Bold, StripOnInput -> False], "\"〉\""}, "RowDefault"]}, 
                            "RowDefault"], " ", TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"〈\"", "5"}, 
                              "RowDefault"], "\"|\"", SubscriptBox["p", "1"], "\"|\"", TemplateBox[
                              {"4", "\"]\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"], " ", TemplateBox[
                            {TemplateBox[{"\"〈\"", "5"}, "RowDefault"], "\"|\"", SubscriptBox[
                              "p", "2"], "\"|\"", TemplateBox[{"3", "\"]\""}, "RowDefault"]}, 
                            "RowDefault"]}], TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"[\"", "4"}, 
                            "RowDefault"], "\"|\"", SubscriptBox["p", "1"], SubscriptBox["p", 
                            RowBox[{"4", ",", "5"}]], "\"|\"", TemplateBox[{"3", "\"]\""}, 
                            "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"]]}], ")"}]}], RowBox[
                   {RowBox[{"(", RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], "+", 
                        SubsuperscriptBox["p", RowBox[{"1", ",", "4"}], "2"]}], ")"}], " ", 
                    RowBox[{"(", RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], "+", 
                        SubsuperscriptBox["p", RowBox[{"2", ",", "3"}], "2"]}], ")"}], " ", 
                    TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"〈\"", "5"}, "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[
                       {"3", "\"〉\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"], " ", TemplateBox[
                     {TemplateBox[{"\"〈\"", "5"}, "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[{"4", "\"〉\""}, 
                       "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"]}]]}], ")"}]}], "Me"], "-", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", SqrtBox["2"], " ", SuperscriptBox["EE", "3"], " ", "Me", " ", 
            TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"〈\"", StyleBox["1", Bold, StripOnInput -> False]}, 
               "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[{StyleBox["2", Bold, StripOnInput -> False], "\"〉\""}, 
               "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"], " ", RowBox[{"(", RowBox[{FractionBox[
                 RowBox[{RowBox[{"(", RowBox[{"1", "+", FractionBox[RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", 
                            SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], "+", SubsuperscriptBox["p", RowBox[
                            {"1", ",", "3"}], "2"]}], RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", 
                             "2"]}], "+", SubsuperscriptBox["p", RowBox[{"1", ",", "5"}], "2"]}]], 
                       "+", FractionBox[RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], "+", 
                          SubsuperscriptBox["p", RowBox[{"2", ",", "4"}], "2"]}], RowBox[
                         {RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], "+", SubsuperscriptBox["p", 
                           RowBox[{"2", ",", "5"}], "2"]}]]}], ")"}], " ", SuperscriptBox[
                    TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"[\"", "3"}, "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[
                       {"4", "\"]\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"], "4"]}], RowBox[
                  {"2", " ", RowBox[{"(", RowBox[{RowBox[{SubscriptBox["p", "3"], ".", SubscriptBox[
                          "p", "4"]}], "+", RowBox[{SubscriptBox["p", "3"], ".", SubscriptBox["p", 
                          "5"]}], "+", RowBox[{SubscriptBox["p", "4"], ".", SubscriptBox["p", 
                          "5"]}]}], ")"}], " ", TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"[\"", "3"}, 
                      "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[{"5", "\"]\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"], 
                   " ", TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"[\"", "5"}, "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[
                      {"4", "\"]\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"], " ", TemplateBox[
                    {TemplateBox[{"\"[\"", "3"}, "RowDefault"], "\"|\"", SubscriptBox["p", "1"], 
                     SubscriptBox["p", RowBox[{"3", ",", "5"}]], "\"|\"", TemplateBox[
                      {"4", "\"]\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"]}]], "+", FractionBox[
                 RowBox[{RowBox[{"(", RowBox[{"1", "+", FractionBox[RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", 
                            SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], "+", SubsuperscriptBox["p", RowBox[
                            {"1", ",", "4"}], "2"]}], RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", 
                             "2"]}], "+", SubsuperscriptBox["p", RowBox[{"1", ",", "5"}], "2"]}]], 
                       "+", FractionBox[RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], "+", 
                          SubsuperscriptBox["p", RowBox[{"2", ",", "3"}], "2"]}], RowBox[
                         {RowBox[{"-", SuperscriptBox["Me", "2"]}], "+", SubsuperscriptBox["p", 
                           RowBox[{"2", ",", "5"}], "2"]}]]}], ")"}], " ", SuperscriptBox[
                    TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"[\"", "4"}, "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[
                       {"3", "\"]\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"], "4"]}], RowBox[
                  {"2", " ", RowBox[{"(", RowBox[{RowBox[{SubscriptBox["p", "3"], ".", SubscriptBox[
                          "p", "4"]}], "+", RowBox[{SubscriptBox["p", "3"], ".", SubscriptBox["p", 
                          "5"]}], "+", RowBox[{SubscriptBox["p", "4"], ".", SubscriptBox["p", 
                          "5"]}]}], ")"}], " ", TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"[\"", "4"}, 
                      "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[{"5", "\"]\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"], 
                   " ", TemplateBox[{TemplateBox[{"\"[\"", "5"}, "RowDefault"], TemplateBox[
                      {"3", "\"]\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"], " ", TemplateBox[
                    {TemplateBox[{"\"[\"", "4"}, "RowDefault"], "\"|\"", SubscriptBox["p", "1"], 
                     SubscriptBox["p", RowBox[{"4", ",", "5"}]], "\"|\"", TemplateBox[
                      {"3", "\"]\""}, "RowDefault"]}, "RowDefault"]}]]}], ")"}]}]}]], "Output"]}, 
     Closed]], Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["From Scoped Numerator Shells To A Complete Amplitude", 
       "Subsection"], Cell["For each positive order (i,j), group (i,5,j), (5,i,j), (i,j,5), whose \
original denominators are Ai Bj, A5 Bj, Ai B5. Their reciprocal sum is Cij/(Ai Bj), without any \
on-shell substitution. After stripping the common factor 2 Sqrt[2] EE^3, the universal numerator \
n=Fi Gj/(Me Gamma) (V-U Fi Gj/Dij) matches each actual diagram on its own two internal numerator \
shells. Generic two-component checks \
passed for all six diagrams and all four independent massive-spin components.", "Text"], 
      Cell["Dij=Ai[ij]+Fi[5j]=Bj[ij]+Gj[i5] explains the distinct three-point-current limits. The \
original denominators are kept opaque during these checks. The completion numerator carries Ai Bj \
when written over that pair's propagators, so it is invisible on the relevant double cuts. Matching \
those residues alone cannot determine this additional off-shell information. It was fixed and \
checked with the independent full Dirac calculation below, not by imposing internal cuts on a \
combined sum.", "Text"]}, Closed]], 
   Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Explicit Cancellation Of The Spurious Poles", "Subsection"], 
      Cell["For one ordered pair put x=Fi Gj, b=[ij], h=[i5][5j], A=Ai, B=Bj, D=Dij, T=[i|p1 k5|j]. \
The two elementary identities are S x-L D=-Me^2 Gamma b^2 and A B b^2+D(T-b B)=h x. They require \
only external shells and conservation. The U coefficient R=-x^2/(A B Gamma D)-Me^2 b^4/(S h D) \
therefore becomes -x L/(A B Gamma S)+Me^2 b^2(T-b B)/(A B S h): D cancels explicitly before the two \
orders are added.", "Text"], Cell["The remaining two scalar sums are: Sum[Cij Rij]=(F3^2 K4/B4+F4^2 \
K3/B3+Me^2[34]^2 L/B5)/(A3 A4 A5), and Sum[Cij Fi Gj/(Ai Bj \
Gamma)]=(-F3[35]K4/B4-F4[45]K3/B3+Me^2[34]^2(A5+B5)/B5)/(A3 A4 A5). Their right sides have physical \
poles only. Multiplying by U,V respectively and adding gives q5MixedFinal.", "Text"], 
      Cell["A hand proof of both sums is included in Section 10 of the PDF. It uses the generic \
chart lambda3=(1,0), lambda4=(0,1), lambda5=(1,1), tilde3=(1,0), tilde4=(0,r), tilde5=(s,t), \
p1={{u,v},{w,z}}, p2=-p1-Sum[ki]. The sole remaining shell equation is E=r+ru+rs-vs+t+ut-wt+z+sz=0, \
with Me^2=uz-vw. The code below independently clears denominators and tests polynomial remainders \
modulo E. No internal shell is used in this equality proof.", "Text"], 
      Cell["ClearAll[q5MPVerifyEquality];\nq5MPVerifyEquality[] := Module[\n  {j = {{0, -1}, {1, \
0}}, eps, adj, la, ti, p, an, sq, f, g, a, b,\n   d, t, c, k, ell, mass2, s, gap, closure, zero, u, \
v, w, z, r, x, y,\n   orders = {{3, 4}, {4, 3}}, localChecks, spuriousU, regularU, spuriousV,\n   \
compactU, compactV, aa, bose, swap},\n  eps = -j;\n  adj[q_] := {{q[[2, 2]], -q[[1, 2]]}, {-q[[2, \
1]], q[[1, 1]]}};\n  la[3] = {1, 0}; la[4] = {0, 1}; la[5] = {1, 1};\n  ti[3] = {1, 0}; ti[4] = {0, \
r}; ti[5] = {x, y};\n  p[1] = {{u, v}, {w, z}};\n  Do[p[i] = Outer[Times, la[i], ti[i]], {i, {3, 4, \
5}}];\n  p[2] = -p[1] - Total[p /@ {3, 4, 5}];\n  mass2 = Det[p[1]]; closure = Expand[Det[p[2]] - \
mass2];\n  zero[q_] := Last[PolynomialReduce[Expand[Numerator[Together[q]]],\n      {closure}, {z, \
w, v, u, y, x, r}]] === 0;\n  an[i_, h_] := la[i].j.la[h]; sq[i_, h_] := ti[i].eps.ti[h];\n  f[i_] \
:= la[5].j.p[1].eps.ti[i];\n  g[i_] := la[5].j.p[2].eps.ti[i];\n  a[i_] := ti[i].adj[p[1]].la[i]; \
b[i_] := ti[i].adj[p[2]].la[i];\n  d[i_, h_] := ti[i].adj[p[1]].(p[i] + p[5]).eps.ti[h];\n  t[i_, \
h_] := ti[i].adj[p[1]].p[5].eps.ti[h];\n  c[i_, h_] := 1 + a[i]/a[5] + b[h]/b[5];\n  k[i_] := \
ti[i].adj[p[1]].p[2].eps.ti[i];\n  ell = la[5].j.p[1].adj[p[2]].la[5];\n  s = Det[p[1] + p[2]]; gap \
= an[5, 3] an[5, 4];\n  localChecks = Function[ord, With[{i = ord[[1]], h = ord[[2]]},\n      \
<|\"Order\" -> ord,\n        \"DLeft\" -> zero[d[i, h] - a[i] sq[i, h] - f[i] sq[5, h]],\n        \
\"DRight\" -> zero[d[i, h] - b[h] sq[i, h] - g[h] sq[i, 5]],\n        \"PoleRemovalIdentity\" -> \
zero[s f[i] g[h] - ell d[i, h] +\n          mass2 gap sq[i, h]^2],\n        \"ProductIdentity\" -> \
zero[a[i] b[h] sq[i, h]^2 +\n          d[i, h] (t[i, h] - sq[i, h] b[h]) -\n          sq[i, 5] \
sq[5, h] f[i] g[h]]|>]] /@ orders;\n  spuriousU = Total[Function[ord, With[{i = ord[[1]], h = \
ord[[2]]},\n      c[i, h] (-f[i]^2 g[h]^2/(a[i] b[h] gap d[i, h]) -\n        mass2 sq[i, h]^4/(s \
sq[i, 5] sq[5, h] d[i, h]))]] /@ orders];\n  regularU = Total[Function[ord, With[{i = ord[[1]], h = \
ord[[2]]},\n      c[i, h] (-f[i] g[h] ell/(a[i] b[h] gap s) +\n        mass2 sq[i, h]^2 (t[i, h] - \
sq[i, h] b[h])/\n          (a[i] b[h] sq[i, 5] sq[5, h] s))]] /@ orders];\n  spuriousV = \
Total[Function[ord, With[{i = ord[[1]], h = ord[[2]]},\n      c[i, h] f[i] g[h]/(a[i] b[h] gap)]] \
/@ orders];\n  aa = a[3] a[4] a[5];\n  compactU = (f[3]^2 k[4]/b[4] + f[4]^2 k[3]/b[3] +\n      \
mass2 sq[3, 4]^2 ell/b[5])/aa;\n  compactV = (-f[3] sq[3, 5] k[4]/b[4] - f[4] sq[4, 5] k[3]/b[3] \
+\n      mass2 sq[3, 4]^2 (a[5] + b[5])/b[5])/aa;\n  <|\"ExternalClosure\" -> closure,\n    \
\"InternalConditionsUsedInEqualityProof\" -> {},\n    \"LocalIdentities\" -> localChecks,\n    \
\"RemoveDPoles\" -> zero[spuriousU - regularU],\n    \"UEqualsThreeTermForm\" -> zero[regularU - \
compactU],\n    \"VEqualsThreeTermForm\" -> zero[spuriousV - compactV],\n    \
\"FullEqualityForArbitraryMassiveSpins\" ->\n      (zero[spuriousU - compactU] && zero[spuriousV - \
compactV])|>\n];\nq5MixedEqualityProof = q5MPVerifyEquality[];\nq5MixedEqualityProof", "Input"], 
      Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"", RowBox[{RowBox[{"\"ExternalClosure\"", "", 
              RowBox[{"r$17183", "+", RowBox[{"r$17183", " ", "u$17183"}], "+", 
                RowBox[{"r$17183", " ", "x$17183"}], "-", RowBox[{"v$17183", " ", "x$17183"}], "+", 
                "y$17183", "+", RowBox[{"u$17183", " ", "y$17183"}], "-", RowBox[{"w$17183", " ", 
                  "y$17183"}], "+", "z$17183", "+", RowBox[{"x$17183", " ", "z$17183"}]}]}], ",", 
            RowBox[{"\"InternalConditionsUsedInEqualityProof\"", "", RowBox[{"{", "}"}]}], ",", 
            RowBox[{"\"LocalIdentities\"", "", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{RowBox[{"", 
                    RowBox[{RowBox[{"\"Order\"", "", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"3", ",", "4"}], 
                          "}"}]}], ",", RowBox[{"\"DLeft\"", "", "True"}], ",", RowBox[
                       {"\"DRight\"", "", "True"}], ",", RowBox[{"\"PoleRemovalIdentity\"", 
                        "", "True"}], ",", RowBox[{"\"ProductIdentity\"", "", "True"}]}], 
                    ""}], ",", RowBox[{"", RowBox[{RowBox[{"\"Order\"", "", RowBox[
                         {"{", RowBox[{"4", ",", "3"}], "}"}]}], ",", RowBox[{"\"DLeft\"", "", 
                        "True"}], ",", RowBox[{"\"DRight\"", "", "True"}], ",", RowBox[
                       {"\"PoleRemovalIdentity\"", "", "True"}], ",", RowBox[
                       {"\"ProductIdentity\"", "", "True"}]}], ""}]}], "}"}]}], ",", 
            RowBox[{"\"RemoveDPoles\"", "", "True"}], ",", RowBox[{"\"UEqualsThreeTermForm\"", 
              "", "True"}], ",", RowBox[{"\"VEqualsThreeTermForm\"", "", "True"}], ",", 
            RowBox[{"\"FullEqualityForArbitraryMassiveSpins\"", "", "True"}]}], ""}]], 
       "Output"]}, Closed]], Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Independent Six-Diagram Dirac Verification", 
       "Subsection"], Cell["This self-contained exact matrix calculation evaluates the six ordinary \
QED diagrams with p1-based references. These references have only physical Ai denominators. All \
four external massive-spin tensor entries agree with q5MixedFinal. The negative-helicity \
polarization phase is calibrated uniformly to the HEPCAT double-cut residues. The code states its \
phase explicitly and uses no model, scratch files, neural net, or internal cut conditions.", 
       "Text"], Cell["ClearAll[q5MPVerifyDirac];\nq5MPVerifyDirac[] := Module[\n  {jform, lform, \
adj, slash, lambda, tilde, photons, p1, p2, massSquared,\n   externalClosure, a, b, aProduct, \
bProduct, physicalDenominator,\n   polarizationNumerator, leftScaled, rightScaled, \
diracNumerator,\n   diracMassReduced, f, kchain, angleChain, square, compactU, compactV,\n   \
externalV, compactCleared, numerator, remainder, spinChecks,\n   u, v, w, z, r, s, t, m, ii, jj},\n \
 jform = {{0, -1}, {1, 0}};\n  lform = -jform;\n  adj[p_] := {{p[[2, 2]], -p[[1, 2]]}, {-p[[2, 1]], \
p[[1, 1]]}};\n  slash[p_] := ArrayFlatten[{\n    {ConstantArray[0, {2, 2}], p},\n    {adj[p], \
ConstantArray[0, {2, 2}]}}];\n  lambda = <|3 -> {1, 0}, 4 -> {0, 1}, 5 -> {1, 1}|>;\n  tilde = <|3 \
-> {1, 0}, 4 -> {0, r}, 5 -> {s, t}|>;\n  photons = AssociationThread[{3, 4, 5},\n    \
Table[Outer[Times, lambda[h], tilde[h]], {h, {3, 4, 5}}]];\n  p1 = {{u, v}, {w, z}};\n  p2 = -p1 - \
Total[Values[photons]];\n  massSquared = Det[p1];\n  externalClosure = Expand[Det[p2] - \
massSquared];\n  a[h_] := Expand[Det[p1 + photons[h]] - massSquared];\n  b[h_] := Expand[Det[p2 + \
photons[h]] - Det[p2]];\n  aProduct = Times @@ (a /@ {3, 4, 5});\n  bProduct = Times @@ (b /@ {3, \
4, 5});\n  physicalDenominator = aProduct bProduct;\n\n  (* Divide these matrices by A_h and \
multiply by Sqrt[2] to obtain\n     the polarization matrices in the stated Dirac convention. *)\n  \
polarizationNumerator[h_] := If[h === 5,\n    -Outer[Times, lambda[h], lambda[h].jform.p1],\n    \
-p1.lform.Outer[Times, tilde[h], tilde[h]]];\n  leftScaled = Join[m jform, \
Transpose[lform.adj[p1]], 2];\n  rightScaled = Join[m IdentityMatrix[2], -adj[p2]];\n\n  (* The two \
scaled external blocks are m times the ordinary external\n     Dirac spinors. Each term's original \
propagators remain A_a B_c. *)\n  diracNumerator = Total[Map[Function[order,\n    With[{aa = \
order[[1]], bb = order[[2]], cc = order[[3]]},\n      \
leftScaled.slash[polarizationNumerator[aa]].\n        (slash[p1 + photons[aa]] + m \
IdentityMatrix[4]).\n        slash[polarizationNumerator[bb]].\n        (slash[p1 + photons[aa] + \
photons[bb]] + m IdentityMatrix[4]).\n        slash[polarizationNumerator[cc]].rightScaled *\n      \
  a[bb] a[cc] b[aa] b[bb]]], Permutations[{3, 4, 5}]]];\n  diracMassReduced = Map[\n    \
Cancel[PolynomialRemainder[Expand[#], m^2 - massSquared, m]/m] &,\n    diracNumerator, {2}];\n\n  \
f[h_] := lambda[5].jform.p1.lform.tilde[h];\n  kchain[h_] := tilde[h].adj[p1].p2.lform.tilde[h];\n  \
angleChain = lambda[5].jform.p1.adj[p2].lambda[5];\n  square[h_, q_] := tilde[h].lform.tilde[q];\n  \
compactU = (f[3]^2 kchain[4]/b[4] + f[4]^2 kchain[3]/b[3] +\n    massSquared square[3, 4]^2 \
angleChain/b[5])/aProduct;\n  compactV = (-f[3] kchain[4] square[3, 5]/b[4] -\n    f[4] kchain[3] \
square[4, 5]/b[3] +\n    massSquared square[3, 4]^2 (a[5] + b[5])/b[5])/aProduct;\n  externalV = \
Outer[Times, lambda[5].jform, lambda[5].jform];\n  compactCleared = aProduct physicalDenominator \
*\n    (compactU jform + compactV externalV);\n\n  (* The plus sign below tests Compact = -Dirac. \
This is the one global\n     phase fixed by the independent HEPCAT double-cut calibration. *)\n  \
spinChecks = Table[\n    numerator = Numerator[Together[\n      diracMassReduced[[ii, jj]] + \
compactCleared[[ii, jj]]]];\n    remainder = Last[PolynomialReduce[Expand[numerator],\n      \
{externalClosure}, {z, w, v, u, t, s, r}]];\n    remainder === 0, {ii, 2}, {jj, 2}];\n  \
<|\"FourIndependentSpinComponents\" -> spinChecks,\n    \"AllPass\" -> And @@ \
Flatten[spinChecks],\n    \"ExternalConditions\" ->\n      \"p1+p2+k3+k4+k5=0; m^2=det(p1); \
det(p2)-det(p1)=0\",\n    \"InternalCutConditionsUsed\" -> None,\n    \
\"ClearedDenominatorConvention\" ->\n      \"D=A3 A4 A5 B3 B4 B5. With N_D built from the scaled \
external blocks, M_Dirac=2 Sqrt[2] e^3 N_D/(m^2 (A3 A4 A5) D). After reducing m^2=det(p1), the \
polynomial tested is N_D/m+(A3 A4 A5)D(c_U J+c_V V5). No internal A_i or B_i is set to zero.\",\n   \
 \"PhaseConvention\" ->\n      \"The displayed compact HEPCAT result equals minus the Dirac sum \
with these polarization matrices. Reversing the negative-helicity polarization sign gives direct \
equality. This phase is fixed by the separate HEPCAT double-cut calibration.\",\n    \
\"ProofMethod\" ->\n      \"Exact rational numerator clearing and polynomial reduction by the \
single external equal-mass condition, for all four independent massive-spin \
components.\"|>\n];\nq5MixedDiracProof = q5MPVerifyDirac[];\nq5MixedDiracProof", "Input"], 
      Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"", RowBox[{RowBox[{"\"FourIndependentSpinComponents\"", "", 
              RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"True", ",", "True"}], "}"}], ",", 
                  RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"True", ",", "True"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", 
            RowBox[{"\"AllPass\"", "", "True"}], ",", RowBox[{"\"ExternalConditions\"", "", 
              "\"p1+p2+k3+k4+k5=0; m^2=det(p1); det(p2)-det(p1)=0\""}], ",", 
            RowBox[{"\"InternalCutConditionsUsed\"", "", "None"}], ",", 
            RowBox[{"\"ClearedDenominatorConvention\"", "", "\"D=A3 A4 A5 B3 B4 B5. With N_D \
built from the scaled external blocks, M_Dirac=2 Sqrt[2] e^3 N_D/(m^2 (A3 A4 A5) D). After reducing \
m^2=det(p1), the polynomial tested is N_D/m+(A3 A4 A5)D(c_U J+c_V V5). No internal A_i or B_i is \
set to zero.\""}], ",", RowBox[{"\"PhaseConvention\"", "", "\"The displayed compact HEPCAT \
result equals minus the Dirac sum with these polarization matrices. Reversing the negative-helicity \
polarization sign gives direct equality. This phase is fixed by the separate HEPCAT double-cut \
calibration.\""}], ",", RowBox[{"\"ProofMethod\"", "", "\"Exact rational numerator clearing and \
polynomial reduction by the single external equal-mass condition, for all four independent \
massive-spin components.\""}]}], ""}]], "Output"]}, Closed]], 
   Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Raw Reference Dependence: A Concrete Counterexample", "Subsection"], 
      Cell["Take Me=1, photon spinors as in the chart with r=4,s=2,t=-25/2, p1={{3,-2},{2,-1}}, \
p2={{-6,29/2},{-4,19/2}}. Both determinants are 1. The original propagators are A={-1,12,-21/2}, \
B={19/2,-24,15}, all nonzero. With both positive references lambda5 and negative square reference \
(1,chi), the actual raw T11 for massive angle components (1,0),(1,0) and their Dirac square \
partners is -32 Sqrt[2] EE^3(2865+772 chi)/(665(25+4 chi)). Its difference from chi=0 is -7168 \
Sqrt[2] EE^3 chi/(475(25+4 chi)), not zero. The reference is regular away from chi=-25/4.", 
       "Text"], Cell["This is an obstruction to treating the raw constructive sum as a \
gauge-independent off-shell amplitude, not a failure of the scoped on-shell identities. The seed, \
raw sum, and completed physical expression are distinct objects. No package source was changed for \
this derivation.", "Text"]}, Closed]], Cell["At a spurious zero in q5MixedSpurious, evaluate \
q5MixedFinal instead of substituting into individual divergent summands. The complete derivation, \
including the short coefficient-by-coefficient proof, is in QED-5-point-reference-derivations.pdf. \
The factored form was also cross-checked against Das and Zeng, arXiv:2608.18218v1, Eqs. (44), (45), \
(75), with labels (1,2,3,4,5)_paper=(1,3,5,4,2)_here and the phase fixed by HEPCAT residues.", 
    "Text"]}, Open]]
},
